'', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5acb841c-be89-583c-a534-80652e454be9', 'word_count': 553, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5acb841c-be89-583c-a534-80652e454be9'}, {'abstract': 'Venezuela has become just the latest victim of hyperinflation — that perfect storm of economic mismanagement, consumer anxiety and political chaos.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/01/magazine/venezuela-inflation-economics.html', 'snippet': 'Venezuela has become just the latest victim of hyperinflation — that perfect storm of economic mismanagement, consumer anxiety and political chaos.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I walked into the empty restaurant in Managua carrying a backpack stuffed with cash, thick stacks of Nicaraguan córdobas bound by rubber bands. The waiter, as expected, asked me to hand over the entire stash. It may have looked like an illicit transaction. But this was Nicaragua, in 1990, at the end of its war with the American-trained contra rebels, and I was only trying to buy a meal before my money lost its value. A decade of guerrilla war and deficit spending had whipped up a maelstrom of hyperinflation and shortages. Only two items on the menu were available, and prices had doubled in a matter of weeks. With inflation surging past 13,000 percent annually, the restaurant now demanded payment upfront — to ensure that the staff had enough time to tally it. As I ate my rice and beans, two waiters at another table counted every bill. I finished before they did, even though the meal — and all those millions of córdobas — added up to less than $10.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 685}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 897, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1923, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/magazine/04mag-onmoney-image1/04mag-onmoney-image1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What 52,000 Percent Inflation Can Do to a Country', 'kicker': 'On Money', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What 52,000 Percent Inflation Can Do to a Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Venezuela', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inflation (Economics)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Economic Conditions and Trends', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Currency', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lenin, Vladimir', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maduro, Nicolas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARGENTINA', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nicaragua', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Weimar (Germany)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'International Monetary Fund', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Citgo Petroleum Corp', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-01T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brook Larmer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brook', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Larmer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ebd4ddc-431b-57e1-9317-0a2b8d511d9e', 'word_count': 1533, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ebd4ddc-431b-57e1-9317-0a2b8d511d9e'}, {'abstract': 'The Norwegian capital is filled with art and stunning architecture, but nature, too, is an integral part of urban life. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/01/travel/what-to-do-in-oslo.html', 'snippet': 'The Norwegian capital is filled with art and stunning architecture, but nature, too, is an integral part of urban life. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oslo is one of Europe’s fastest growing capitals and it shows. Nestled between pristine forests and a fjord, this compact Norwegian city has long been recognized for its cultural institutions and its dedication to environmental sustainability (it’s the European Green Capital for 2019). But in the decade since the completion of the landmark opera house, Norway’s forward-thinking capital has worked to make compelling architecture its new calling card. Herds of construction cranes swing above the harbor, and entire neighborhoods like the futuristic Barcode district — a row of distinctive side-by-side high-rises — have sprouted. Go now to witness the city’s reinvention in progress, from a newly vibrant downtown to its redrawn skyline. It won’t look like this for long.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Hours-Oslo2/merlin_145888866_690ad0bc-8c95-40bb-8fcf-0bd41bb87de0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Hours-Oslo2/merlin_145888866_690ad0bc-8c95-40bb-8fcf-0bd41bb87de0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Hours-Oslo2/merlin_145888866_690ad0bc-8c95-40bb-8fcf-0bd41bb87de0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Hours-Oslo2/merlin_145888866_690ad0bc-8c95-40bb-8fcf-0bd41bb87de0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1484, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Hours-Oslo2/11Hours-Oslo2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Hours-Oslo2/11Hours-Oslo2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption':