ws', '_id': 'nyt://article/6795d81b-67f6-587a-a6bf-2e48c5428f45', 'word_count': 1717, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6795d81b-67f6-587a-a6bf-2e48c5428f45'}, {'abstract': 'I hate that it has been so completely taken over by loud angry white guys. And yet late at night, I still listen. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/01/opinion/am-radio-coast-to-coast.html', 'snippet': 'I hate that it has been so completely taken over by loud angry white guys. And yet late at night, I still listen. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Like many people who grew up in the 1970s, I came of age with AM radio. Everybody I knew — the black kids on my block, the white and Asian kids at my junior high school — followed the Top 40 and discussed the merits of the newest releases by Elton John and Eddie Kendricks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/opinion/01Kaplan3/01Kaplan3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/01/opinion/01Kaplan3/01Kaplan3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/opinion/01Kaplan3/01Kaplan3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/opinion/01Kaplan3/01Kaplan3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/opinion/01Kaplan3/01Kaplan3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {