y Cuddy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cuddy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2bea13cd-1e17-5b75-a0d8-4a2a4aab5788', 'word_count': 1013, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2bea13cd-1e17-5b75-a0d8-4a2a4aab5788'}, {'abstract': 'I should feel safer, but the president’s anti-immigrant rhetoric doesn’t help.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/03/opinion/sunday/immigration-el-salvador-trump-united-states.html', 'snippet': 'I should feel safer, but the president’s anti-immigrant rhetoric doesn’t help.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My best friends and I try to camp on a Northern California river every summer, in the hopes it becomes tradition. We have done it three of the past four years. This year, because the Russian River was low, we went westward from our usual spot. On our way, we drove past a house with a Confederate flag flying over it. My friends are white; I am not. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/opinion/sunday/04zamora/04zamora-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/04/opinion/sunday/04zamora/04zamora-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/opinion/sunday/04zamora/04zamora-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/04/opinion/sunday/04zamora/04zamora-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}