ane Flanagan — in third place.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/04/sports/nyc-marathon-womens-winners.html', 'snippet': 'Four of the top seven finishers in the women’s race were American, including last year’s winner — Shalane Flanagan — in third place.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mary Keitany was back where she prefers to be Sunday in the New York City Marathon — far, far ahead of everyone else. Keitany, an Olympian from Kenya, took off alone in the race’s second half and finished more than three minutes ahead of her challengers, with a time of 2 hours 22 minutes 48 seconds. It was her fourth victory here, and the second fastest race any woman has run on this course.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/sports/05marathon-women-hp1/05marathon-women-hp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/05/sports/05marathon-women-hp1/05marathon-women-hp1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/sports/05marathon-women-hp1/05marathon-women-hp1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/sports/05marathon-women-hp1/05marathon-women-hp1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/sports/05marathon-women-hp1/05marathon-women-hp1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '