k': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG/05tmag-ballet-slide-19DG-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Gay Male Ballet Dancers, in Photos', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMERICAN BALLET THEATER', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Boston Ballet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Ballet', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York City Ballet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hoven, Blaine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Janzen, Russell', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Royal, Calvin III', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sebastian, Jose (Dancer)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stanley, Taylor (1991- )', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whiteside, James', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-05T10:10:14+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/bb1fcdd8-63bb-5dde-a41a-3da855d47e73', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/bb1fcdd8-63bb-5dde-a41a-3da855d47e73'}, {'abstract': 'These men are finding new stages on which to express their queerness, collapsing gender barriers in the world of dance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/t-magazine/gay-male-ballet-dancers.html', 'snippet': 'These men are finding new stages on which to express their queerness, collapsing gender barriers in the world of dance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When I was 15, I met a dancer from Canada’s Royal Winnipeg Ballet. The company had come to Los Angeles to dance in the Olympic Arts Festival, and my parents volunteered to host a post-performance dinner in our backyard. I recall about 200 people — family friends, Olympic officials and maybe 25 dancers — eating curry (is that right?) off paper plates. But that’s not what this is about. No, this is about the ballerino — my word for him — I met and what he represented to a lonely gay kid in Southern California in 1984, a kid who had never before met another gay person. Earlier that evening, I had seen the dancer turn, leap and smile onstage, expressing through the mute language of ballet who he was. Something about his movement told me he was gay, and I felt he was dancing not only for himself but for me. Onstage, the ballerino wore brown tights that showed the trunks of his thighs, and everything else. Now he was in loose linen pants with a drawstring belt and an open collar that exposed the rod of his clavicle.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '51', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/t-magazine/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1/05tmag-ballet-slide-19A1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How a Group of Gay Male Ballet Dancers Is Rethinking Masculinity', 'kicker': 'Arts and Letters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Man’s Job', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dancing', '