'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sauna With an Observation Deck, Dreamed Up at a Designers’ Retreat ', 'kicker': 'Other Rooms', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'One Extraordinary (And Totally Nonessential) Space. Now Visiting: A Sauna on Gotland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Saunas and Sweat Lodges', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Royal College of Art (London)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gotland Island (Sweden)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-05T17:24:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nancy Hass', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nancy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hass', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c506ded-cc08-5d02-b403-99ac287f1d00', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c506ded-cc08-5d02-b403-99ac287f1d00'}, {'abstract': 'Robin Standefer, a co-founder of the Manhattan interior design company Roman and Williams, first encountered the specialized dish in the ’90s.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/t-magazine/robin-standefer-roman-williams-oyster-plate-collection.html', 'snippet': 'Robin Standefer, a co-founder of the Manhattan interior design company Roman and Williams, first encountered the specialized dish in the ’90s.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Robin Standefer, who (with husband Stephen Alesch) founded the Manhattan interior design company Roman and Williams (their projects include New York City’s High Line Hotel and Upland restaurant), first encountered Victorian oyster plates as a 29-year-old consultant on Martin Scorsese’s 1993 film “The Age of Innocence.” Her job was locating Gilded Age table settings, and these majolica shellfish plates made in Staffordshire, England, by Minton were a must-have in upper-class homes of the 1860s on both sides of the Atlantic. A few years ago, when Roman and Williams were asked to redo the British galleries at the Metropolitan Museum of Art, she saw the plates again and began collecting. Today, Standefer has amassed 20 of the jewel-tone platters, with their sea-creature embellishments and contoured divots (you shuck the bivalves and slide them onto the plate, shell-less). Recently, she has put a few up for sale at the Guild, a retail outpost she and Alesch opened last year in SoHo. “They’re magical,” she says, “and tell a story of the world at a certain time.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '170', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/02/t-magazine/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/02/t-magazine/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/02/t-magazine/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 748, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/02/t-magazine/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 747, 'width': 748, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/02/t-magazine/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF/02tmag-plates-slide-2WIF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 't