302c', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0015978-3bbc-5fba-b9d1-9d681a70302c'}, {'abstract': 'KellyBronze heritage turkeys are heading to the Chelsea Market, just in time for Thanksgiving. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/dining/kellybronze-turkey.html', 'snippet': 'KellyBronze heritage turkeys are heading to the Chelsea Market, just in time for Thanksgiving. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'For several generations, KellyBronze heritage turkeys have been bred in England and preferred by chefs like Jamie Oliver. In 2014, the company established a 130-acre farm in Crozet, in the Blue Ridge Mountains of Virginia, and it is the only commercial turkey farm that holds a Department of Agriculture license to dry-age and hand-pluck its birds. The free-roaming pampered turkeys, more flavorful than the average bird, are available somewhat more widely this year, always fresh, from the company’s website and, for New Yorkers, at Dickson’s Farmstand Meats in Chelsea Market. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/dining/07burner7/07burner7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/07/dining/07burner7/07burner7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/dining/07burner7/07burner7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/dining/07burner7/07burner7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None,