-479f91fe05bc'}, {'abstract': 'In a significant propaganda shift, Xi Jinping’s rise has come at the expense of Deng Xiaoping, long hailed as the architect of China’s prosperity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/world/asia/china-xi-jinping-deng-xiaoping.html', 'snippet': 'In a significant propaganda shift, Xi Jinping’s rise has come at the expense of Deng Xiaoping, long hailed as the architect of China’s prosperity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SHENZHEN, China — Shortly after taking over as China’s leader, Xi Jinping made a pilgrimage to lay a wreath at a large bronze monument to one of his predecessors, the man credited with ushering in the country’s new era of capitalist prosperity 40 years ago, Deng Xiaoping.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/merlin_129349823_4091635a-4b6e-44a4-84c6-9384fb288be3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/merlin_129349823_4091635a-4b6e-44a4-84c6-9384fb288be3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/merlin_129349823_4091635a-4b6e-44a4-84c6-9384fb288be3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/merlin_129349823_4091635a-4b6e-44a4-84c6-9384fb288be3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/01china-deng-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/01china-deng-2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/01/world/01china-deng-2/01china-deng-2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'China’s Leader, Hogging Spotlight, Elbows Communist Titan Aside', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'China’s Leader, Hogging Spotlight, Elbows Communist Titan Aside', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Xi Jinping', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Deng Xiaoping', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-05T21:02:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Lee Myers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': 'Lee', 'lastname': 'Myers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5840ca22-801d-516e-acf5-eb15af1bac86', 'word_count': 1237, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5840ca22-801d-516e-acf5-eb15af1bac86'}, {'abstract': 'The president’s unrelenting focus on migrants may prove ineffective because voters have already sorted themselves out along partisan lines.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/opinion/its-not-easy-to-predict-how-immigration-will-affect-the-midterms.html', 'snippet': 'The president’s unrelenting focus on migrants may prove ineffective because voters have already sorted themselves out along partisan lines.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the closing days of the campaign for the midterms, President Trump has clearly decided that immigration should be the central issue of this election. Mr. Trump called a caravan of Central Americans heading toward the United States it “an assault on our country” and asserted without evidence that it includes “bad people” and “unknown Middle Easterners.” He accused Democrats of having “something to do with it.” He floated the idea of ending birthright citizenship for children born in the United States to undocumented immigrants. He circulated an ad about a Mexican man convicted of killing two police officers that said, “Democrats let him into our country.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/30/opinion/30sides/merlin_144570840_a9c63382-2a7f-4884-977a-9d5310db3cd0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/30/opinion/30sides/merlin_144570840_a9c63382-2a7f-4884-977a-9d5310db3cd0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/30/opinion/30sides/merlin_144570840_a9c63382-2a7f-4884-977a-9d5310db3cd0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/30/opinion/30sides/merlin_144570840_a9c63382-2a7f-4884-977a-9d5310db3cd0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1331, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'ima