, 'lastname': 'Vavreck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/703ab50d-417c-558b-99d5-ac8c6601f642', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/703ab50d-417c-558b-99d5-ac8c6601f642'}, {'abstract': 'In Obama’s era, democracy done in good faith struggled. For his demagoguing opponents, that remains the whole point. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/opinion/politics/obama-2008-election-ballot-trump.html', 'snippet': 'In Obama’s era, democracy done in good faith struggled. For his demagoguing opponents, that remains the whole point. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ten years ago yesterday, 240,000 spectators nestled in Chicago’s Grant Park and millions tuning in worldwide huddled together and watched a lithe, elegant African-American man stroll victoriously across a shimmering stage with his beautiful young family to accept the challenge of leading the free world. He opened his speech wryly asking, “If there is anyone out there who still doubts that America is a place where all things are possible, who still wonders if the dream of our founders is alive in our time, who still questions the power of our democracy, tonight is your answer.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Suskind1/merlin_25727331_0116b9a5-44fd-41b2-8583-cd3aceaf8024-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Suskind1/merlin_25727331_0116b9a5-44fd-41b2-8583-cd3aceaf8024-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Suskind1/merlin_25727331_0116b9a5-44fd-41b2-8583-cd3aceaf8024-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 10