er a response to Trumpian nationalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'National identity is the most powerful force in world politics today. Most of the strong leaders around the world were swept to power with a strong nationalist story and govern in nationalist ways. This is true in Russia, China, India, the U.S., Israel, Turkey, Britain, Brazil and on and on. It’s hard to see how any party could appeal or govern these days without a strong national story.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/merlin_146364702_2dab0f35-23f6-4f9c-a635-a16ce114a396-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/merlin_146364702_2dab0f35-23f6-4f9c-a635-a16ce114a396-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/merlin_146364702_2dab0f35-23f6-4f9c-a635-a16ce114a396-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/merlin_146364702_2dab0f35-23f6-4f9c-a635-a16ce114a396-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1319, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/05brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/05brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05brooksWeb/05brooksWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Do Democrats Know What Unites Us?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Central  Challenge  Of the Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T00:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6dea75d6-bdf3-55f4-904e-e04aa942c5f2', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6dea75d6-bdf3-55f4-904e-e04aa942c5f2'}, {'abstract': 'Stop the bombing and start a large-scale relief effort.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/opinion/yemen-war-saudi-arabia-trump.html', 'snippet': 'Stop the bombing and start a large-scale relief effort.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Though much remains clouded in the murder of the Saudi journalist-in-exile Jamal Khashoggi, this much is clear: Saudi Arabia’s rulers are ruthless and not to be trusted or believed. It is now time to recognize those realities in the kingdom’s unspeakably cruel war in Yemen. The Trump administration has been prodded into demanding a cease-fire, but that seems only to have provoked new fighting. The United States, Britain and other enablers of the Saudi campaign can and must demand an immediate halt to the carnage.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/merlin_145625763_6898df36-322a-41f7-a8ad-c03f4effb40f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/merlin_145625763_6898df36-322a-41f7-a8ad-c03f4effb40f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/merlin_145625763_6898df36-322a-41f7-a8ad-c03f4effb40f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/merlin_145625763_6898df36-322a-41f7-a8ad-c03f4effb40f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/05yemen-edtWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/05yemen-edtWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05yemen-edtWeb/05yemen-edtWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'End Yemen’s Agony', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houthis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khashoggi, Jamal', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed bin Salman (1985- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pompeo, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Iran', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T00:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/dcb554d2-433a-5c62-bfb8-6fd647bdf436', 'word_count': 780, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dcb554d2-433a-5c62-bfb8-6fd647bdf436'}, {'abstract': 'A marine biologist, Dr. Gates worked to develop a “super coral” to resist the deadening effects of warming ocean waters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/obituaries/ruth-gates-dead-marine-biologist-who-championed-coral.html', 'snippet': 'A marine biologist, Dr. Gates worked to develop a “super coral” to resist the deadening effects of warming ocean waters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ruth Gates, a renowned marine biologist who made it her life’s work to save the world’s fragile coral reefs from the deadening effects of warming water temperatures, died on Oct. 25 in Kailua, Hawaii. She was 56.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/merlin_146139462_32bc67fa-8daa-47f6-966a-adc6f6526117-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/merlin_146139462_32bc67fa-8daa-47f6-966a-adc6f6526117-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/merlin_146139462_32bc67fa-8daa-47f6-966a-adc6f6526117-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/merlin_146139462_32bc67fa-8daa-47f6-966a-adc6f6526117-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/00GATES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/00GATES1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/obituaries/06GATES1/00GATES1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Ruth Gates, Who Made Saving Coral Reefs Her Mission, Is Dead at 56', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Ruth Gates, a Champion of Coral Reefs in a Time of Their Decline, Dies at 56', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gates, Ruth (1962-2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coral', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Reefs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marine Biology', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'University of Hawaii', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hawaii Institute of Marine Biology', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T00:09:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Obituaries', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katharine Q. Seelye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katharine', 'middlename': 'Q.', 'lastname': 'Seelye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/40de9d31-aca3-5f5a-8432-d1242327809f', 'word_count': 1014, 'uri': 'nyt://article/40de9d31-aca3-5f5a-8432-d1242327809f'}, {'abstract': 'More than 100 years ago, black domestic workers in Georgia organized for better pay. Now they’re getting out the vote for a groundbreaking candidate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/05/opinion/atlanta-domestic-workers-vote-stacey-abrams.html', 'snippet': 'More than 100 years ago, black domestic workers in Georgia organized for better pay. Now they’re getting out the vote for a groundbreaking candidate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'All across Atlanta, hundreds of domestic workers have been knocking on doors for Stacey Abrams, the Democratic candidate for Georgia governor, hoping to turn her into first black woman in that role. ', 'source':