'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5403e203-67a1-5d04-8c07-3737cc6b05e3'}, {'abstract': 'With millions of Americans taking risky medications for questionable diagnoses, have we medicalized everyday life?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/well/live/a-profusion-of-diagnoses-thats-good-and-bad.html', 'snippet': 'With millions of Americans taking risky medications for questionable diagnoses, have we medicalized everyday life?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I recently cared for a hairdresser who had gone through a year of vague and varied symptoms. What started as a few unpleasant aches soon became debilitating pain throughout her body. A heavy fatigue settled into her bones: Holding scissors or sweeping the floor became too much. She slept fitfully; her memory flagged. Frustrated by many symptoms and few answers, she grew anxious and depressed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 547, 'width': 780, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2015/11/20/science/welldoctor/welldoctor-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Profusion of Diagnoses. That’s Good and Bad.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Depression (Mental)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fibromyalgia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Insomnia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Testosterone', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Attention Deficit Hyperactivity Disorder', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Live', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dhruv Khullar, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dhruv', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Khullar', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/76eda9a7-792e-5349-b58e-ee4c90f0b81d', 'word_count': 994, 'uri': 'nyt://article/76eda9a7-792e-5349-b58e-ee4c90f0b81d'}, {'abstract': 'Cranberry jam, lemon curd and ginger turn this typically warm-weather dessert into a fall or winter treat.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/magazine/eton-mess-dessert-fall-winter.html', 'snippet': 'Cranberry jam, lemon curd and ginger turn this typically warm-weather dessert into a fall or winter treat.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I got my first baking job through a friend of a friend of a friend and lost it a month or so later. I had no experience as a baker, no training, but I got lucky: The restaurant, the long-gone Soho Charcuterie, needed an extra pair of hands when my name came up. I was hired on the spot and given two specific jobs to do each day: make 100 chocolate cookies and bake a few chocolate cakes with whiskey and raisins. As both of the house specialties were similar to recipes I’d made at home, all went well. And then, one day, I had what I thought was a good idea. Without telling anyone, I made the cake with a few changes: I substituted Armagnac for the whiskey, pecans for the almonds, and prunes, not everyone’s favorite fruit, for the raisins. That’s when I was fired for “creative insubordination.” If I’d been less defeated, I might have seen that the real reason I was fired was that I was caught being myself.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1103, 'width': 1550, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7/11mag-dessert-slide-MVM7-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Eton Mess, a Classic Dessert for Endless Variation', 'kicker': 'On Dessert', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Confessions of an Inveterate Fiddler', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Desserts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dorie Greenspan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dorie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenspan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c1549ae-6afa-59cd-adfb-f6b8a879bd64', 'word_count': 853, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c1549ae-6afa-59cd-adfb-f6b8a879bd64'}, {'abstract': 'What’s labeled as for men or for women doesn’t have to be.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-womens-clothing.html', 'snippet': 'What’s labeled as for men or for women doesn’t have to be.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last year, I walked into an upscale independent clothing store in Berlin and greeted the conservatively dressed, bespectacled woman hovering in the back. I’d seen a stylish male mannequin in the window, but it wasn’t clear that they sold men’s clothing, so I asked. “It’s all for everyone,” she said. “I mean, technically that rack and this rack are men’s, but I believe it’s outdated to think like that.” ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-jumbo.png', 'height': 745, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-LOR-1/11mag-LOR-1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Women’s Clothing', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Women’s Clothing', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kalle Oskari Mattila', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kalle', 'middlename': 'Oskari', 'lastname': 'Mattila', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63288e4e-02bd-54ee-a88f-5cb11b5fc697', 'word_count': 938, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63288e4e-02bd-54ee-a88f-5cb11b5fc697'}, {'abstract': 'The new president of Planned Parenthood on patient advocacy, conspiracy theories and why it’s insulting when anti-choicers call themselves “pro-life.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/magazine/dr-leana-wen-dislikes-the-politicization-of-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'The new president of Planned Parenthood on patient advocacy, conspiracy theories and why it’s insulting when anti-choicers call themselves “pro-life.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'You are the new president of Planned Parenthood. What were some of your first exposures to the clinic? My mom was a patient when I was a kid, and I volunteered as a patient escort when I was a medical student. I remember thinking: What kind of world do we live in where, in order to get health care, women — and men, but mainly women — have to walk through lines of protesters? The politicization of care deeply troubles me. That’s, unfortunately, the reality that we’re in.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '74', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/magazine/11mag-talk-image2/11mag-talk-image2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dr. Leana Wen Dislikes the Politicization of Health Care', 'kicker': 'Talk', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dr. Leana Wen Dislikes the Politicization of Health Care', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birth Control and Family Planning', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wen, Leana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Planned Parenthood Federation of America', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Caitlin  Roper', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Caitlin', 'lastname': 'Roper', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9a9ebf26-fa26-5498-a708-c93e6a781cfb', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9a9ebf26-fa26-5498-a708-c93e6a781cfb'}, {'abstract': 'Dickens began his novel in the marshes of the Hoo Peninsula, about 25 miles from London. More than 150 years later, a traveler retraces the path of that book’s indelible characters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/travel/pip-and-me-a-journey-into-the-world-of-great-expectations.html', 'snippet': 'Dickens began his novel in the marshes of the Hoo Peninsula, about 25 miles from London. More than 150 years later, a traveler retraces the path of that book’s indelible characters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a warm morning, the sky is cloudless and the marshes of the Hoo Peninsula, 25 miles downriver from London, are thick with daises and red clover. In the churchyard of St Mary’s in the village of Lower Higham there is a scent of cut grass. The whole scene, in other words, is distinctly un-Dickensian. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge