 {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Blackburn, Marsha', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bredesen, Phil', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gingrich, Newt', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Waters, Maxine', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gail Collins and Bret Stephens', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Bret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stephens', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1592cfd-18aa-57ce-9002-081321803e03', 'word_count': 1781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1592cfd-18aa-57ce-9002-081321803e03'}, {'abstract': 'The lying, misogyny, racism and attacks on the rule of law from our president are awakening the vast middle of American politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/opinion/james-comey-election-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The lying, misogyny, racism and attacks on the rule of law from our president are awakening the vast middle of American politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’ve been traveling around the United States for six months speaking about ethical leadership. Nearly every place I go, I hear some version of this question: “Are we going to be O.K.?” What the questioner means is, given the current leadership of our country and the ugly undercurrent on which it thrives, is America as we know it going to survive? Yes, is the answer I give, without hesitation. We will recover. How long that takes is up to us, but I am optimistic.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/merlin_146341389_13703d42-6b7b-48ba-a9a3-2cbee590bc47-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/merlin_146341389_13703d42-6b7b-48ba-a9a3-2cbee590bc47-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/merlin_146341389_13703d42-6b7b-48ba-a9a3-2cbee590bc47-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/merlin_146341389_13703d42-6b7b-48ba-a9a3-2cbee590bc47-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1153, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/05Comey2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/05Comey2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/05/opinion/05Comey2/05Comey2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'James Comey: Let’s Vote to Uphold Our Nation’s Values', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Zigzag Path to a Better Country', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meacham, Jon', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Higher Loyalty: Truth, Lies, and Leadership (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Nineteen Hundred Twenties', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T11:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Comey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Comey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f4736435-83f5-588f-abac-47894106185e', 'word_count': 760, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f4736435-83f5-588f-abac-47894106185e'}, {'abstract': 'Young voters discuss the issues motivating them this year.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/opinion/midterm-elections-young-voters.html', 'snippet': 'Young voters discuss the issues motivating them this year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Young people historically vote at lower rates, typically, than other age groups, and that has been especially true of the midterms. But this year, registration for younger voters is up substantially, with some studies anticipating the highest youth turnout in decades. We wanted to know what issues are motivating young people at such impressive rates this year, so we asked. In just a few days we had more than 800 passionate, sharp and often surprising responses.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/05youngams-voting/05youngams-voting-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/05youngams-voting/05youngams-voting-articleLarge.gi