://article/fafbde4a-99b4-51eb-9e3a-0c867fc3f724'}, {'abstract': 'Adriaen Block calls itself the first restaurant and bar in New York City to serve food and drinks infused with cannabidiol. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/style/cbd-cocktail-bar-adriaen-block.html', 'snippet': 'Adriaen Block calls itself the first restaurant and bar in New York City to serve food and drinks infused with cannabidiol. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'There are CBD massage parlors, CBD bakeries and even CBD cafes. So it was only matter of time before a bar would join this bandwagon. Adriaen Block, which opened in August, bills itself as the first CBD restaurant and bar in New York City, with four lower-alcohol cocktails infused with cannabidiol derived from hemp.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/merlin_143017299_4f645249-3e32-4710-9ecb-716705fb1fbb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/merlin_143017299_4f645249-3e32-4710-9ecb-716705fb1fbb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/merlin_143017299_4f645249-3e32-4710-9ecb-716705fb1fbb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/merlin_143017299_4f645249-3e32-4710-9ecb-716705fb1fbb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/08BOITE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/08BOITE-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/fashion/08BOITE-1/08BOITE-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Queens Bar That Serves CBD-Infused Cocktails ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Adriaen Block | Astoria, Queens', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bars and Nightclubs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-onlyinnewyork', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T15:45:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian Sloan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sloan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9165b220-9705-5a47-ae43-dc483d692842', 'word_count': 451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9165b220-9705-5a47-ae43-dc483d692842'}, {'abstract': 'Among the areas experiencing problems were polling places in Georgia as Election Day voting began in the race for governor between Brian Kemp and Stacey Abrams.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/us/politics/voting-issues-election-day-georgia.html', 'snippet': 'Among the areas experiencing problems were polling places in Georgia as Election Day voting began in the race for governor between Brian Kemp and Stacey Abrams.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From closed polling sites to malfunctioning machines, Election Day brought frustration for some voters in contests shadowed by questions about the security and fairness of the electoral system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/07vote-problems2/07vote-problems2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Voting Problems Surface as Americans Go to the Polls', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting Machines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abrams, Stacey Y', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemp, Brian P', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Gwinnett County (Ga)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T15:45:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Danny Hakim, Alan Blinder and Michael Wines', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Danny', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hakim', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wines', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6862a26-3421-51a3-84dd-a66fedabbac5', 'word_count': 1620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6862a26-3421-51a3-84dd-a66fedabbac5'}, {'abstract': 'If Utah legalizes medical marijuana on Tuesday, it could signal that the church is no longer all-powerful in state politics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/opinion/mormon-church-medical-marijuana-utah-referendum.html', 'snippet': 'If Utah legalizes medical marijuana on Tuesday, it could signal that the church is no longer all-powerful in state politics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SALT LAKE CITY — In September, a billboard appeared near downtown here urging voters to support Proposition 2, an initiative to legalize medical marijuana that is on the ballot Tuesday. Quoting from Mormon Church scripture and its “word of wisdom” about food and drink, the billboard read, “All Wholesome Herbs God Has Ordained for the Use of Man.” In other words, you can use pot for your medical ills and still be a good Mormon. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/merlin_140744577_3ea70ed9-04fd-4dee-b76d-fce9eb06b0f5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/merlin_140744577_3ea70ed9-04fd-4dee-b76d-fce9eb06b0f5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/merlin_140744577_3ea70ed9-04fd-4dee-b76d-fce9eb06b0f5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 629, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/merlin_140744577_3ea70ed9-04fd-4dee-b76d-fce9eb06b0f5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1258, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/06morgan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/06morgan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06morgan/06morgan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mormon Church vs. Pot', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Referendums', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mormons (Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-Day Saints)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medical Marijuana', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Marijuana Policy Project', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Love, Mia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salt Lake City (Utah)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Utah', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T16:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. Kael Weston', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': 'Kael', 'lastname': 'Weston', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/4997d493-e81f-573f-a9fa-51adc648cc8b', 'word_count': 1023, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4997d493-e81f-573f-a9fa-51adc648cc8b'}, {'abstract': 'The region’s democratic systems have been tested by many authoritarian rulers throughout history. But lines of defense against its challengers often do their job. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/opinion/can-latin-american-democracy-withstand-the-populist-assault.html', 'snippet': 'The region’s democratic systems have been tested by many authoritarian rulers throughout history. But lines of defense against its challengers often do their job. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'AMHERST, Mass. — It is common to think of Latin America as the land of no hope for democracy. Since independence, the region has been ravaged by authoritarianism and populism. Brazil’s new president-elect, Jair Bolsonaro, an ex-military macho promising zero tolerance of everything he dislikes, evokes a “here we go again” feeling. Once again, illiberalism seems ascendant, to the detriment of democracy.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 407, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 407}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 695, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1390, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06corrales/06corrales-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can Latin American Democracy Withstand the Populist Assault? ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Defying Latin America’s Strongmen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Term Limits (Political Office)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolsonaro, Jair (1955- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chavez, Hugo', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T16:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Javier Corrales', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Javier', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Corrales', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1ce3dc87-7711-5a42-8e17-4f5288a44550', 'word_count': 1048, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1ce3dc87-7711-5a42-8e17-4f5288a44550'}, {'abstract': 'Aqueous abstraction meets barefoot modernism in the Brooklyn home of the couple behind Eskayel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/t-magazine/eskayel-shanan-campanaro-nick-chacona-williamsburg-loft.html', 'snippet': 'Aqueous abstraction meets barefoot modernism in the Brooklyn home of the couple behind Eskayel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'AFTER TOSSING OUT her furniture following a bad breakup with her live-in boyfriend in 2006, Shanan Campanaro, a California-bred artist and graphic designer based in Brooklyn, needed something to mask the emptiness. So the Central Saint Martins graduate took one of the paintings she had been working on in her spare time — a set of antlers rendered in watery ink, from a series about headpieces from crowns to coxcombs — and digitally printed it onto a roll of paper in close repeats. The resulting wallpaper, which evoked the claustrophobic horror vacui of Victorian interiors, thrilled everyone who saw it and became the first pattern produced by Eskayel, the now 10-year-old wallpaper and design company Campanaro runs with her husband, Nick Chacona.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '80', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 430, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 430}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1467, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/t-magazine/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ/06tmag-prints-slide-R7HQ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Inside an Airy Williamsburg Loft Where Patterns Run Wild', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Color of Water', 'name':