at charges, if any, will be brought in the case, officials said on Tuesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/merlin_130069019_6e62fb5e-3231-48ae-89a0-607cc7aed958-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 772, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/merlin_130069019_6e62fb5e-3231-48ae-89a0-607cc7aed958-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 772}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/merlin_130069019_6e62fb5e-3231-48ae-89a0-607cc7aed958-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 796, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/merlin_130069019_6e62fb5e-3231-48ae-89a0-607cc7aed958-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1230, 'width': 956, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/07dc-commando-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/07dc-commando-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/07/us/politics/07dc-commando/07dc-commando-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Navy Completes Inquiry Into Strangling Death of Army Green Beret in Mali', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Navy Sends Homicide Report to Admiral', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Navy Seals', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mali', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Melgar, Logan J (1983-2017)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-06T19:52:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Africa', 'byline': {'original': 'By Eric Schmitt', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Eric', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schmitt', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d8f520d-3973-5cba-ac89-c3add90bc441', 'word_count': 826, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d8f520d-3973-5cba-ac89-c3add90bc441'}, {'abstract': 'Tech companies and their employees love big cities, but Amazon needs to do better for people who live in any city chosen for its second headquarters.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/06/opinion/amazon-hq2-split.html', 'snippet': 'Tech companies and their employees love big cities, but Amazon needs to do better for people who live in any city chosen for its second headquarters.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The prune capital of America. That was the future Silicon Valley’s greatest claim to fame in the 1920s, when it was a sleepy landscape of fruit orchards and farms far removed from the nation’s industrial might. Seattle was a city of fishing and timber, where a young entrepreneur named Bill Boeing had so few customers for his airplanes that he briefly pivoted to making furniture. The most innovative companies in the world clustered in the ferociously inventive cities of the East and Midwest — cars in Detroit; cash registers in Dayton, Ohio; light bulbs in Cleveland.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '33', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/merlin_129983582_59950200-ac42-401b-b473-6391961f0366-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/merlin_129983582_59950200-ac42-401b-b473-6391961f0366-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/merlin_129983582_59950200-ac42-401b-b473-6391961f0366-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/merlin_129983582_59950200-ac42-401b-b473-6391961f0366-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/06omaraWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/06omaraWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/06/opinion/06omaraWeb/06omaraWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Warning From Seattle to Amazon’s HQ2 ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Brace Yourself For HQ2', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name