}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a198c565-c692-5e46-bb3a-bfb5135817dd', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a198c565-c692-5e46-bb3a-bfb5135817dd'}, {'abstract': 'The apps and strategies for singles, families and flexible travelers who want to beat the crowds to the slopes, and still not pay too much.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/07/travel/ski-for-less-budget.html', 'snippet': 'The apps and strategies for singles, families and flexible travelers who want to beat the crowds to the slopes, and still not pay too much.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If I may borrow a phrase: Winter is coming. And with that comes holidays, family gatherings and vacation time. Ski vacations are certainly popular during the winter months, but they’re not always easy to plan. Furthermore, prepping for a ski getaway can vary wildly, depending on whether you’re a single professional or a couple with children; if you’re hemmed in by specific dates or have a good deal of flexibility in your schedule. Below are tips for your next ski trip no matter what your profile — and while it won’t necessarily be cheap, there are ways to make it more affordable.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/merlin_130586882_db107d3b-407b-4b44-b9eb-49e56b146623-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/merlin_130586882_db107d3b-407b-4b44-b9eb-49e56b146623-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/merlin_130586882_db107d3b-407b-4b44-b9eb-49e56b146623-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/merlin_130586882_db107d3b-407b-4b44-b9eb-49e56b146623-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/11Frugal-winterski1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/11Frugal-winterski1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/travel/11Frugal-winterski1/11Frugal-winterski1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Ski for Less This Winter', 'kicker': 'Frugal traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Break Your Budget for a Skiing Adventure', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skiing', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-07T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Peterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5ba8c45c-d63d-511a-91c1-20c7a193979c', 'word_count': 1523, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5ba8c45c-d63d-511a-91c1-20c7a193979c'}, {'abstract': 'Site details? Incentives? Much of the process has been secret, and local officials and developers signed nondisclosure agreements.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/07/technology/amazon-hq2-know.html', 'snippet': 'Site details? Incentives? Much of the process has been secret, and local officials and developers signed nondisclosure agreements.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SEATTLE — For more than a year, Amazon searched for a second headquarters, a home to as many as 50,000 workers that would be coequal to its current home in Seattle. Instead, Amazon is closing in on deals to split what it called HQ2 into two locations, according to people briefed on the discussions. The company appears ready to move to Long Island City in Queens, according to two of the people. It is also close to a deal to move to a spot in Arlington, Va., just across the Potomac River from Washington, one of the people said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/business/08amazonexplain/08amazonexplain-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 373, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/08/business/08amazonexplain/08amazonexplain-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 373}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/business/08amazonexplain/08amazonexplain-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/business/08amazonexplain/08amazonexplain-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1273, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'i