://article/c480bf7d-16c8-50d0-a328-3d0b969a870f'}, {'abstract': 'For more than 50 years she harangued executives, sometimes wearing a costume to make a point. And sometimes this gadfly got results.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/07/business/evelyn-davis-dead.html', 'snippet': 'For more than 50 years she harangued executives, sometimes wearing a costume to make a point. And sometimes this gadfly got results.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Evelyn Y. Davis, who spent more than 50 years haranguing American executives at shareholder meetings as she pushed companies to be more frugal and transparent, died on Sunday in Washington. She was 89.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/merlin_146415276_37997e5c-73e7-4bd0-ac95-0aab5a6c7af4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 864, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/merlin_146415276_37997e5c-73e7-4bd0-ac95-0aab5a6c7af4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 864}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/merlin_146415276_37997e5c-73e7-4bd0-ac95-0aab5a6c7af4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 712, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/merlin_146415276_37997e5c-73e7-4bd0-ac95-0aab5a6c7af4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1423, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/07DAVIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/07DAVIS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/obituaries/08DAVIS1/07DAVIS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Evelyn Y. Davis, Shareholder Scourge of C.E.O.s, Dies at 89', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Evelyn Y. Davis, Gadfly Shareholder Whose Antics Got Results, Is Dead at 89', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Davis, Evelyn Y', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shareholder Rights and Activism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-07T18:58:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily Flitter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Flitter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/749ba016-66e9-53ce-b86b-bd2f5a8cf075', 'word_count': 1210, 'uri': 'nyt://article/749ba016-66e9-53ce-b86b-bd2f5a8cf075'}, {'abstract': 'Video games and novels have more in common than you might think. Jeremy Klemin explains how the logic of both involves enigmas and resolutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/07/books/review/pokemon-video-game-logic.html', 'snippet': 'Video games and novels have more in common than you might think. Jeremy Klemin explains how the logic of both involves enigmas and resolutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Between the ages of 5 and 10, I spent many solitary weekends at my grandparents’ house reading middle grade books and playing Pokémon on my Game Boy. The fact that I read one and played the other was unimportant; I was captivated by both in the same way — by how detailed they were, by how even the most trivial bits of information could prove meaningful in the context of their respective narratives. I spent an unjustifiable amount of time not only playing games like Pokémon, but also scouring them for secrets that may or may not have existed. The kinds of rumors that surrounded such games are instantly recognized by most millennials: “You can catch a Mew” — a particularly coveted and elusive Pokémon — “if you can get to the truck next to the S.S. Anne”; “There’s a secret stash of Pokémon behind Bill’s house.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Klemin/merlin_146046864_a62d1452-77fd-4718-b664-c6135a7e24ef-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Klemin/merlin_146046864_a62d1452-77fd-4718-b664-c6135a7e24ef-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Klemin/merlin_146046864_a62d1452-77fd-4718-b664-c6135a7e24ef-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Klemin/merlin_146046864_a62d1452-77fd-4718-b664-c6135a7e24ef-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1236, 'width': 1236, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 's