'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Tomasky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tomasky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/06690e23-0201-5c43-882c-757c9d0e59d7', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/06690e23-0201-5c43-882c-757c9d0e59d7'}, {'abstract': '“A great work is one you never get tired of — you find new value in it every day.” So says this playwright, who has a taste for lyrical realism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/07/arts/design/show-us-your-wall-terrence-mcnally.html', 'snippet': '“A great work is one you never get tired of — you find new value in it every day.” So says this playwright, who has a taste for lyrical realism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Having a documentary made about you can prompt reflection, and “Every Act of Life” is having that effect on its subject, the four-time Tony-winning playwright and librettist Terrence McNally, who just turned 80.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09showwall1/09showwall1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09showwall1/09showwall1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09showwall1/09showwall1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09showwall1/09showwall1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1368, 'subType': 