ontrol in three state capitals was in some cases less a sharp shift on matters of national ideology than a pragmatic tacking to a middle.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LAWRENCE, Kan. — A decade ago, a Democrat was governor of Kansas. And Illinois. And Michigan. And Wisconsin. Since then, Republicans dominated, winning governor’s races across much of the Midwest and enacting conservative policies that reshaped the region in their image.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09midwest-fallout1-print/merlin_146440803_45c99da7-732f-44aa-8316-8ea058e1700b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09midwest-fallout1-print/merlin_146440803_45c99da7-732f-44aa-8316-8ea058e1700b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09midwest-fallout1-print/merlin_146440803_45c99da7-732f-44aa-8316-8ea058e1700b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09midwest-fallout1-print/merlin_146440803_45c99da7-732f-44aa-8316-8ea058e1700b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09midwest-fallout1-print/00midwest-fallout1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09midwest-fallout1-print/00midwest-fallout1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheig