document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Middle East', 'byline': {'original': 'By David M. Halbfinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8430dd9d-a3ac-589f-b01a-eed3183b88d9', 'word_count': 612, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8430dd9d-a3ac-589f-b01a-eed3183b88d9'}, {'abstract': 'Chris Pine stars in a historical slog about Robert the Bruce (1274-1329) that is little more than a churn of mud, entrails and misty nationalism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/08/movies/outlaw-king-review.html', 'snippet': 'Chris Pine stars in a historical slog about Robert the Bruce (1274-1329) that is little more than a churn of mud, entrails and misty nationalism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Why do moviemakers insist on telling historical stories when they’re really just interested in costumes and war? There’s nothing new about the abbreviated history you find in “Outlaw King,” a monotonous slog through the life and brutally terrible times of Robert the Bruce (1274-1329), a Scottish noble who fought — and fought — the English. At least in old Hollywood, filmmakers would also try to entertain you amid the clashes and post-combat huddles, giving you something more to watch and ponder than this movie’s oceans of mud, truckloads of guts and misty, unconsidered nationalism.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/merlin_146195427_d203828a-4d97-4038-8e82-1e39b1a9d144-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/merlin_146195427_d203828a-4d97-4038-8e82-1e39b1a9d144-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/merlin_146195427_d203828a-4d97-4038-8e82-1e39b1a9d144-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/merlin_146195427_d203828a-4d97-4038-8e82-1e39b1a9d144-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/09outlawking-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/09outlawking-2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/arts/09outlawking-2/09outlawking-2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Outlaw King’ Review: Bloody Medieval Times and Guts', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Going Medieval in Embattled Scotland', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dillane, Stephen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mackenzie, David', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pine, Chris', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Outlaw King (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-08T16:45:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/c5a9a494-d1e6-5405-93e6-03bf76b9486a', 'word_count': 646, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c5a9a494-d1e6-5405-93e6-03bf76b9486a'}, {'abstract': 'Starting Nov. 11, “Meanwhile” will be a regular part of the Sunday Business section, exploring the rich story behind an everyday object, familiar place or uncelebrated face.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/08/business/wendy-macnaughton-meanwhile-illustrated-column.html', 'snippet': 'Starting Nov. 11, “Meanwhile” will be a regular part of the Sunday Business section, exploring the rich story behind an everyday object, familiar place or uncelebrated face.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For eight years, my visual storytelling series “Meanwhile” has highlighted overlooked people, places and things that I’m curious about and believe are worthy of our attention. I’ve published a book of these stories, “Meanwhile in San Francisco,” and on the back page of The California Sunday Magazine, my column has examined subjects from prison hospice programs to rockets to nonagenarian besties.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/business/08meanwhile-topart/08meanwhile-topart-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 169, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/17/business/08meanwhile-topart/08meanwhile-topart-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 169}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/business/08meanwhile-topart/08meanwhile-topart-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 288, 'width': 1024, '