agraph': 'ATLANTA — Brian Kemp, the Republican who has claimed victory in the Georgia governor’s race, said on Thursday that he was resigning as secretary of state, removing himself from the process of determining whether he had in fact been elected.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/merlin_146520753_599ee87c-4602-4c0e-a5d4-172bcb5de68e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/merlin_146520753_599ee87c-4602-4c0e-a5d4-172bcb5de68e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/merlin_146520753_599ee87c-4602-4c0e-a5d4-172bcb5de68e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/merlin_146520753_599ee87c-4602-4c0e-a5d4-172bcb5de68e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/09GEORGIA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/09GEORGIA1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/09/us/09GEORGIA1-copy/09GEORGIA1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Brian Kemp Resigns as Georgia Secretary of State, With Governor’s Race Still Disputed', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Governors', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemp, Brian P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Abrams, Stacey Y', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Atlanta (Ga)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crittenden, Robyn A', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-08T17:30:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alan Blinder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blinder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/cf135eaa-2a83-56c6-b6e9-49a0844b82a7', 'word_count': 924, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cf135eaa-2a83-56c6-b6e9-49a0844b82a7'}, {'abstract': 'The president is evading the requirement to seek the Senate’s advice and consent for the nation’s chief law enforcement officer and the person who will oversee the Mueller investigation. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/08/opinion/trump-attorney-general-sessions-unconstitutional.html', 'snippet': 'The president is evading the requirement to seek the Senate’s advice and consent for the nation’s chief law enforcement officer and the person who will oversee the Mueller investigation. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'What now seems an eternity ago, the conservative law professor Steven Calabresi published an op-ed in The Wall Street Journal in May arguing that Robert Mueller’s appointment as special counsel was unconstitutional. His article got a lot of attention, and it wasn’t long before President Trump picked up the argument, tweeting that “the Appointment of the Special Counsel is totally UNCONSTITUTIONAL!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 690, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1379, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/opinion/08Kaytal/08Conway-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Appointment of the Acting Attorney General Is Unconstitutional', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Whitaker’s Appointment Is Illegal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitaker, Matthew G', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-08T17:39:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neal K. Katyal and George T. Conway III', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neal', 'middlename': 'K.', 'lastname': 'Katyal', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'George', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Conway', 'qualifier': 'III', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b8c61e0a-33bc-5685-bbe0-c63ec33d5b55', 'word_count': 1034, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b8c61e0a-33bc-5685-bbe0-c63ec33d5b55'}, {'abstract': 'By studying the relationship among ethnicity, migration history and the digestive system’s microbiome, researchers hope to gain insights on health disparities in diverse communities.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/08/health/immigration-gut-microbiome.html', 'snippet': 'By studying the relationship among ethnicity, migration history and the digestive system’s microbiome, researchers hope to gain insights on health disparities in diverse communities.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bodies that migrate across borders undergo tremendous change. Immediately, feet alight on alien terrain, ears channel novel sounds and noses breathe in unfamiliar scents. More gradually, daily routines fall into new rhythms, cultural norms hybridize and dreams evolve. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/merlin_136310001_1cf9c785-a9b0-42ab-ab65-991d337303fb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 462, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/merlin_136310001_1cf9c785-a9b0-42ab-ab65-991d337303fb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 462}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/merlin_136310001_1cf9c785-a9b0-42ab-ab65-991d337303fb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 788, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/merlin_136310001_1cf9c785-a9b0-42ab-ab65-991d337303fb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1540, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/09TB-MICROBIOME1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/09TB-MICROBIOME1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/science/09TB-MICROBIOME1/09TB-MICROBIOME1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLar