b_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/08/opinion/sunday/criminal-justice-reforms-race-technology.html', 'snippet': 'Recent criminal justice reforms contain the seeds of a frightening system of “e-carceration.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the midterms, Michigan became the first state in the Midwest to legalize marijuana, Florida restored the vote to over 1.4 million people with felony convictions, and Louisiana passed a constitutional amendment requiring unanimous jury verdicts in felony trials. These are the latest examples of the astonishing progress that has been made in the last several years on a wide range of criminal justice issues. Since 2010, when I published “The New Jim Crow” — which argued that a system of legal discrimination and segregation had been born again in this country because of the war on drugs and mass incarceration — there have been significant changes to drug policy, sentencing and re-entry, including “ban the box” initiatives aimed at eliminating barriers to employment for formerly incarcerated people. ', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11alexander/merlin_146497086_4a40c292-16b4-45bd-8c0e-c79c965bdf85-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11alexander/merlin_146497086_4a40c292-16b4-45bd-8c0e-c79c965bdf85-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11alexander/merlin_146497086_4a40c292-16b4-45bd-8c0e-c79c965bdf85-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201