ssions, Jefferson B III', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitaker, Matthew G', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 16, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-09T17:44:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen I. Vladeck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': 'I.', 'lastname': 'Vladeck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cde1a5c9-57ea-58e1-a1e5-3095dbde07d2', 'word_count': 1144, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cde1a5c9-57ea-58e1-a1e5-3095dbde07d2'}, {'abstract': 'Maithripala Sirisena’s move, which critics said was illegal, deepened a two-week-old constitutional crisis over who is the legitimate prime minister of the island nation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/world/asia/sri-lanka-dissolves-parliament.html', 'snippet': 'Maithripala Sirisena’s move, which critics said was illegal, deepened a two-week-old constitutional crisis over who is the legitimate prime minister of the island nation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'COLOMBO, Sri Lanka — The president of Sri Lanka dissolved the country’s Parliament on Friday night and called for elections in January to choose new lawmakers, a move that critics said was illegal, and that deepened a two-week-old constitutional crisis over who is the legitimate prime minister of the island nation.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/world/10lanka/10lanka-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/10/world/10lanka/10lanka-articl