om/2018/11/09/business/media/trump-retaliation-reporters-april-ryan.html', 'snippet': 'The president, speaking on the South Lawn before leaving for a brief jaunt to Paris, also targeted the reporter April D. Ryan with an unprompted diatribe in which he called her a “loser.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Trump said on Friday that he might revoke the credentials of additional White House reporters if they did not “treat the White House with respect,” lobbing another threat at the news media two days after his administration effectively blacklisted the CNN correspondent Jim Acosta.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Threatens to Retaliate Against Reporters Who Don’t Show ‘Respect’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump May Blacklist More Reporters Who Don’t Show ‘Respect’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CNN', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'American Urban Radio Network', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Public Broadcasting Service', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alcindor, Yamiche', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Acosta, Jim', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ryan, April D', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Phillip, Abby (Journalist)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-09T18:06:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Media', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael M. Grynbaum', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c8319f09-e7b9-52ca-af4b-49c58238094a', 'word_count': 769, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c8319f09-e7b9-52ca-af4b-49c58238094a'}, {'abstract': 'These books for young vehicle lovers have it all: size, strength, speed — even kindness. And a dog.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/books/review/kate-prendergast-dog-on-a-digger.html', 'snippet': 'These books for young vehicle lovers have it all: size, strength, speed — even kindness. And a dog.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They HUFF, they ROAR, they CLANK, they MOVE! Size, strength and speed, embodied! No wonder we are most fascinated by vehicles when we ourselves are at our youngest, smallest and least independent. No wonder, too, that there have been picture books about moving machines for about as long as either has been around. (See “Cousin Chatterbox’s Railway Alphabet” from the 1840s for an early example: “U is the urchin, so simple and small, / who cannot make out how the train goes at all.”) New arrivals in this long tradition drive, float and fly onto shelves each publishing season. A kicking of tires follows for some of the latest. As always, your mileage may vary.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Floca-02/merlin_145739364_411ff4f1-64e6-46d3-a35e-b1391191d9c2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 257, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Floca-02/merlin_145739364_411ff4f1-64e6-46d3-a35e-b1391191d9c2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 257}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/books/review/11Floca-02/merlin_145739364_411ff4f1-64e6-46d3-a35e-b1391191d9c2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 43