line': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/fd036d62-6686-5806-9054-b8c73241e64c', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/fd036d62-6686-5806-9054-b8c73241e64c'}, {'abstract': 'The artists Alexander Calder and Ellsworth Kelly maintained an intimate, lively correspondence that reveals affinities both personal and aesthetic.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/t-magazine/alexander-calder-ellsworth-kelly-letters.html', 'snippet': 'The artists Alexander Calder and Ellsworth Kelly maintained an intimate, lively correspondence that reveals affinities both personal and aesthetic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'How is art shaped by friendship? The exhibition “Calder / Kelly,” which is now open at the Lévy Gorvy gallery in New York, entertains this question across three floors of work and ephemera by the artists Alexander Calder and Ellsworth Kelly. Spanning five decades, the pieces highlight the aesthetic and personal affinities between these two heavyweights of 20th-century abstract art. American modernists who both spent formative periods in Paris (in the late 1920s and late 1940s, respectively), Calder and Kelly eventually met in that city and maintained a lasting fondness for one another, despite an age difference of 25 years.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/08/t-magazine/art/Calder-slide-TJZC/Calder-slide-TJZC-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rare Look at the Letters Between Two Art World Giants', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Letters', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Calder, Alexander', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, Ellsworth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Levy Gorvy Gallery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-09T19:46:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Liz Hirsch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Liz', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hirsch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a8dc36e-1edf-59f5-8d83-888f7824cb14', 'word_count': 660, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a8dc36e-1edf-59f5-8d83-888f7824cb14'}, {'abstract': 'As crowds gathered in New York, Paris and London, photographers captured the public’s jubilant mood.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/world/europe/armistice-day-100th-anniversary-photos.html', 'snippet': 'As crowds gathered in New York, Paris and London, photographers captured the public’s jubilant mood.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Great War was over. One hundred years ago — just before 3 a.m. on Nov. 11, 1918 — The New York Times received the first bulletin of the Armistice, which had been signed aboard a rail car in a small village in Northern France. A searchlight on the tower of the Times building, previously used to announce election results, gleamed rays across the city until daylight broke.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/world/11armistice4/merlin_146271387_4b067494-e61b-46ac-8bba-a36d6b1577e1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 435, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/world/11armistice4/merlin_146271387_4b067494-e61b-46ac-8bba-a36d6b1577e1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 435}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/world/11armistice4/merlin_146271387_4b067494-e61b-46ac-8bba-a36d6b1577e1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 742, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/world/11armistice4/merlin_146271387_4b067494-e61b-46ac-8bba-a36d6b1577e1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1484, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': 