 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Ian Black', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'Ian', 'lastname': 'Black', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3ccc755c-7a50-54ce-8fa2-be1e05e8b409', 'word_count': 1044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3ccc755c-7a50-54ce-8fa2-be1e05e8b409'}, {'abstract': 'While Ian D. Long may have suffered from PTSD, no evidence has been made public that it was ever diagnosed or that he was treated.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/us/ian-david-long-sexual-assault.html', 'snippet': 'While Ian D. Long may have suffered from PTSD, no evidence has been made public that it was ever diagnosed or that he was treated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the search for answers after a shooting that left 12 people dead at the Borderline Bar & Grill in Thousand Oaks, Calif., much attention has been focused on the gunman’s time in the Marine Corps, wondering if post-traumatic stress disorder from combat in Afghanistan left him primed to kill.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10veterans/merlin_146577942_fbcf4649-561b-40b2-abf1-d5fd166a6c25-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 422, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10veterans/merlin_146577942_fbcf4649-561b-40b2-abf1-d5fd166a6c25-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 422}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10veterans/merlin_146577942_fbcf4649-561b-40b2-abf1-d5fd166a6c25-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 720, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'super