ing', '_id': 'nyt://article/0dedaca8-7d64-5092-9df8-cfaeea6850d9', 'word_count': 1041, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0dedaca8-7d64-5092-9df8-cfaeea6850d9'}, {'abstract': 'Think you are good with a rod? Try catching a fish that supposedly doesn’t even feed in the rivers where it swims in British Columbia.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/sports/steelhead.html', 'snippet': 'Think you are good with a rod? Try catching a fish that supposedly doesn’t even feed in the rivers where it swims in British Columbia.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELKWA, British Columbia — Steelhead are a form of oceangoing rainbow trout endemic to some rivers draining to the Pacific from North America and Russia’s Kamchatka Peninsula. They are also a metaphor for wonder and optimism.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/sports/10steelhead/merlin_146580393_f2a3bef0-cff8-4970-a6f3-25e240a217c8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/10/sports/10steelhead/merlin_146580393_f2a3bef0-cff8-4970-a6f3-25e240a217c8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/sports/10steelhead/merlin_146580393_f2a3bef0-cff8-4970-a6f3-25e240a217c8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/sports/10steelhead/merlin_146580393_f2a3bef0-cff8-4970-a6f3-25e240a217c8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1500, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/