desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Kaplan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaplan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed383819-dcd1-5319-aa29-01e6b68139cf', 'word_count': 928, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed383819-dcd1-5319-aa29-01e6b68139cf'}, {'abstract': 'To the female cross-country runners at the New Jersey school, the decision was infuriating but not surprising.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/sports/rowan-sports-bra-controversy.html', 'snippet': 'To the female cross-country runners at the New Jersey school, the decision was infuriating but not surprising.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was 69 degrees when the Rowan cross-country teams arrived for practice at the Glassboro, N.J., university’s track on Oct. 30. During the workout, several of the male runners removed their shirts. Some members of the women’s team did the same, continuing the session in sports bras.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/autossell/10SPORTSBRA02/merlin_146594343_ceb5fa6f-21f2-49f4-afa7-aa19b697ae41-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/10/autossell/10SPORTSBRA02/merlin_146594343_ceb5fa6f-21f2-49f4-afa7-aa19b697ae41-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/autossell/10SPORTSBRA02/merlin_146594343_ceb5fa6f-21f2-49f4-afa7-aa19b697ae41-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty