iddlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dwyer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90819a92-b40e-5222-b33f-c330aa43b4df', 'word_count': 415, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90819a92-b40e-5222-b33f-c330aa43b4df'}, {'abstract': 'The Democratic candidate hopes to force a runoff in Georgia’s race for governor. The state is still locked in a tight contest.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/09/us/georgia-governor-abrams-kemp.html', 'snippet': 'The Democratic candidate hopes to force a runoff in Georgia’s race for governor. The state is still locked in a tight contest.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ATLANTA — The allies of Stacey Abrams, the Democratic candidate trailing in the Georgia governor’s race, hit the streets and the phones on Friday in a vigorous last-minute push to get anyone who cast a provisional ballot to ensure that their vote would count, in the hopes of forcing the close, bitter and expensive contest into a runoff.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10GEORGIA1/merlin_146586285_fdf11c91-6b0b-4969-88a7-ed7be07277ff-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10GEORGIA1/merlin_146586285_fdf11c91-6b0b-4969-88a7-ed7be07277ff-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10GEORGIA1/merlin_146586285_fdf11c91-6b0b-4969-88a7-ed7be07277ff-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/10/us/10GEORGIA1/merlin_14658628