.", 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/10/opinion/sunday/american-germany-public-school-funding.html', 'snippet': "In Germany, my daughter’s school offered circus lessons. Now I'll have to sell wrapping paper to keep the gym lights on.", 'lead_paragraph': 'After almost six years in Munich, my family and I will soon be returning to California, and there are a few things I already know I will miss. I am not talking about the obvious (fresh pretzels, fresh pretzels with cheese, fresh pretzels with cheese and pumpkin seeds, no potholes, universal health care) but the less known differences that come with spending time in schools.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 376, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 376}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 642, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1283, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11dumas/11dumas-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why I Dread Returning to an American Public School', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Will Miss You, German Schools', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Munich (Germany)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-10T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Firoozeh Dumas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Firoozeh', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dumas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/9317d238-dbca-5d31-9ebd-aa4bb492bf38', 'word_count': 874, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9317d238-dbca-5d31-9ebd-aa4bb492bf38'}, {'abstract': 'In the 1930s it contributed to the rise of fascism. Alarmingly, we are experimenting again with a monopolized economy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/10/opinion/sunday/fascism-economy-monopoly.html', 'snippet': 'In the 1930s it contributed to the rise of fascism. Alarmingly, we are experimenting again with a monopolized economy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the aftermath of the Second World War, an urgent question presented itself: How can we prevent the rise of fascism from happening again? If over the years that question became one of mostly historical interest, it has again become pressing, with the growing success of populist, nationalist and even neofascist movements all around the world.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/merlin_146593434_598a9ae9-8595-4674-94c9-ddcac6ba8355-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/merlin_146593434_598a9ae9-8595-4674-94c9-ddcac6ba8355-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 421}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/merlin_146593434_598a9ae9-8595-4674-94c9-ddcac6ba8355-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 719, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/merlin_146593434_598a9ae9-8595-4674-94c9-ddcac6ba8355-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1439, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/11wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/11wu-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11wu/11wu-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Be Afraid of Economic ‘Bigness.’ Be Very Afraid.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Be Afraid of Economic ‘Bigness.’ Be Very Afraid.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-10T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tim Wu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e06ca3ff-956f-5aa3-835d-8803e7c49909', 'word_count': 1303, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e06ca3ff-956f-5aa3-835d-8803e7c49909'}, {'abstract': 'Where your brain goes when you’re asleep helps you when you’re awake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/10/opinion/sunday/dreams-meaning-science.html', 'snippet': 'Where your brain goes when you’re asleep helps you when you’re awake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One muggy Saturday last summer, I went on a date with a man who seemed entirely fine. We drank two beers and went for a walk, and he explained why he liked certain buildings that we passed. We kissed, and his breath tasted like cigarettes. We parted ways, and I couldn’t muster the energy to answer his emoji-laden follow-up texts about my weekend activities.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 641, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 641}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 959, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1918, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11robb/11robb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Do You Keep Dreaming You Forgot Your Pants? It’s Science', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Your Dreams Tell You Who You Are', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dreams', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Anxiety and Stress', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sleep', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emotions', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-10T19:30:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alice Robb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alice', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Robb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f1f70e12-a91e-5899-9e2d-97f69504cc5f', 'word_count': 1653, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f1f70e12-a91e-5899-9e2d-97f69504cc5f'}, {'abstract': 'V.H.A. doctors care for some of America’s most vulnerable. They are not “bad apples” who “rob us or cheat us.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/10/opinion/sunday/veterans-department-health-hospitals.html', 'snippet': 'V.H.A. doctors care for some of America’s most vulnerable. They are not “bad apples” who “rob us or cheat us.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'This Veterans Day, in addition to honoring those who serve in uniform, we should spend some time remembering the 300,000 employees of the Veterans Health Administration. The V.H.A. — the nation’s largest public health system — doesn’t just keep veterans healthy; it has developed treatments that help all Americans. And if we don’t defend it, it could be dismantled and auctioned off in whatever remains of the Trump era.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11Gordon/merlin_62568971_9dce53e3-b41f-4efa-ac6d-94a308cd843e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11Gordon/merlin_62568971_9dce53e3-b41f-4efa-ac6d-94a308cd843e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11Gordon/merlin_62568971_9dce53e3-b41f-4efa-ac6d-94a308cd843e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/11/opinion/sunday/11Gordon/merlin_62568971_9dce53e3-b41f-4efa-ac6d-94a308cd843e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, '