one, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/345d9214-7cea-519c-ae7b-e5c1e8dde0d5', 'word_count': 526, 'uri': 'nyt://article/345d9214-7cea-519c-ae7b-e5c1e8dde0d5'}, {'abstract': 'She initially avoided writing about the traumas in her life, focusing instead on the food. “Life is too short for even one bad meal,” she wrote.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/11/obituaries/louise-desalvo-dead.html', 'snippet': 'She initially avoided writing about the traumas in her life, focusing instead on the food. “Life is too short for even one bad meal,” she wrote.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Louise A. DeSalvo, a Virginia Woolf scholar and memoirist who mined her Italian-American heritage for her books and who once observed that life “is too short for even one bad meal,” died on Oct. 31 in Montclair, N.J. She was 76.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/obituaries/12DESALVO-OBIT2/09DESALVO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/12/obituaries/12DESALVO-OBIT2/09DESALVO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/obituaries/12DESALVO-OBIT2/09DESALVO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/obituaries/12DESALVO-OBIT2/09DESALVO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url':