btype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/briefing/13briefing-asia/13briefing-asia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/12/briefing/13briefing-asia/13briefing-asia-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/briefing/13briefing-asia/13briefing-asia-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'North Korea, China, Afghanistan: Your Tuesday Briefing', 'kicker': 'Asia and Australia Edition', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-11-12T19:22:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NYTNow', 'section_name': 'Briefing', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alisha Haridasani Gupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alisha', 'middlename': 'Haridasani', 'lastname': 'Gupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'briefing', '_id': 'nyt://article/07bdbecc-4a2e-5746-a04d-8816e3927568', 'word_count': 1208, 'uri': 'nyt://article/07bdbecc-4a2e-5746-a04d-8816e3927568'}, {'abstract': 'In “Let It Bang,” the African-American journalist RJ Young writes of learning about firearms in order to nurture a connection with his white father-in-law.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/12/books/let-it-bang-rj-young-interview.html', 'snippet': 'In “Let It Bang,” the African-American journalist RJ Young writes of learning about firearms in order to nurture a connection with his white father-in-law.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When the African-American journalist RJ Young first met Charles Stafford, the white Oklahoman man who would become his father-in-law for a time, Stafford walked out of the room, came back and handed Young a very large revolver. “I felt certain,” Young writes, “that I had landed in either Wes Craven’s rendition of ‘Guess Who’s Coming to Dinner’ or the next film in the ‘Saw’ franchise.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 883, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 883}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 697, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1902, 'width': 1293, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/books/13fivequestions-young1/13young1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Tell Us 5 Things About Your Book: An Unlikely Relationship With Gun