ine': {'original': 'By Laurie Goodstein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Laurie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goodstein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af41028c-0e66-5784-9831-8de7226a3829', 'word_count': 1236, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af41028c-0e66-5784-9831-8de7226a3829'}, {'abstract': 'For the first time, four of the top elected statewide officials will be women who ran on a broad range of issues.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/12/opinion/election-michigan-women-stabenow-whitmer.html', 'snippet': 'For the first time, four of the top elected statewide officials will be women who ran on a broad range of issues.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The first time I ran for office, for a seat on my county board of commissioners, I was 24 years old. I didn’t have a lot of political experience. What I did have was a cause I believed in — keeping the local nursing home open — and the willingness to work really hard. My opponent in the race, an older male incumbent, derisively referred to me as “that young broad.” That young broad beat him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 428, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 428}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 731, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1462, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12Stabenow/12Stabenow-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Michigan, the Best Candidates Just Happened to Be Women', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Michigan', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Midterm Elections (2018)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Slotkin, Elissa', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tlaib, Rashida', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitmer, Gretchen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stevens, Haley', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-12T20:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Debbie Stabenow', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Debbie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stabenow', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1b34939f-e964-5b97-bda1-e7cd99c93c1b', 'word_count': 578, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1b34939f-e964-5b97-bda1-e7cd99c93c1b'}, {'abstract': 'A growing number of government officials are misusing their office in egregious ways to try to tilt the electoral playing field in their favor. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/12/opinion/florida-rick-scott-georgia-election-results.html', 'snippet': 'A growing number of government officials are misusing their office in egregious ways to try to tilt the electoral playing field in their favor. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sunday, the Republican secretary of state of Arizona, Michele Reagan, did a stunning thing. She explained to America why it was taking so long to count the ballots in Arizona’s unresolved Senate race. Her explanation was thorough, sober, informative and nonpartisan. Most important, it helped foster confidence in the process. It wasn’t just her. Arizona’s Republican governor, Doug Ducey, tweeted over the weekend: “Let’s get this right. All legally cast votes must be counted.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 663, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1326, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/12bassin/12bassin-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re Suing the Florida Governor. He Should Not Oversee His Own Election.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ducey, Doug (1964- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kemp, Brian P', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kobach, Kris W', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scott, Richard L', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ARIZONA', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Georgia', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-12T20:25:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ian Bassin', 'person': [{