agrant green Sichuan peppercorns.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/12/dining/mala-market-sichuan-spices.html', 'snippet': 'The Mala Market carries a dozen essential spices for the fiery cuisine, including fragrant green Sichuan peppercorns.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Sichuan peppercorns, the dried seed pods of the prickly ash, are actually not a kind of pepper, but a spice that delivers tongue-tingling heat with a citrus accent. They have become quite widely available. The ones sold by the Mala Market, a new company in Nashville, are high-quality. Taylor Holliday, the owner, imports the spices directly from the source, so they are fresher than most. She also sells fragrant green Sichuan peppercorns, which deliver a shade less heat but more all-around flavor. A dozen more essentials for Sichuan cooking — like preserved vegetables, chile pods, chile oil, soy sauce, fermented black beans, Chinese vinegar and handmade chile bean paste — are also sold. The website posts recipes, including a terrific one for dry-fried green beans.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/merlin_146485053_6579b5db-c4e4-49f8-a5d1-2446eb62df3a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/merlin_146485053_6579b5db-c4e4-49f8-a5d1-2446eb62df3a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 617}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/merlin_146485053_6579b5db-c4e4-49f8-a5d1-2446eb62df3a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 996, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/merlin_146485053_6579b5db-c4e4-49f8-a5d1-2446eb62df3a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1992, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/14burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/14burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/dining/14burner2/14burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Looking for Sichuan Ingredients? A Nashville Company Delivers', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Amplify: Need Sichuan Ingredients? A Nashville Outfit Delivers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chili Peppers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mala Market, The', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Nashville (Tenn)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-12T21:14:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/906d0763-169f-55c7-889f-c147d7168b5c', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/906d0763-169f-55c7-889f-c147d7168b5c'}, {'abstract': 'Readers are stunned by the president’s tweet blaming the state for the wild