ules.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Decorating a child’s bedroom is hard enough when you have only one child. Add another to the mix and the challenges multiply.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/oakImage-1541790263555-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 387, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/oakImage-1541790263555-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 387}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/oakImage-1541790263555-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 660, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/oakImage-1541790263555-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1320, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/18fix1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/18fix1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/realestate/18fix1/18fix1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Double the Children, Double the Challenge', 'kicker': 'THE FIX', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Double the Children, Multiply the Challenges', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interior Design and Furnishings', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Home Repairs and Improvements', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-13T10:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Higgins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Higgins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9d5be081-eef9-5050-80be-b7c7bfc09794', 'word_count': 1483, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9d5be081-eef9-5050-80be-b7c7bfc09794'}, {'abstract': 'In Istanbul, self-expression can be as simple as the way you tie your hijab, doff your flat cap or always, always dye your hair.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/13/style/cosmopolitan-style-in-turkey.html', 'snippet': 'In Istanbul, self-expression can be as simple as the way you tie your hijab, doff your flat cap or always, always dye your hair.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Betül: I don’t really have a style, I just find something that looks good and I wear it — skinny jeans, mom jeans. Usually, I match my hijab to my clothes. I have about 20 or 25 and they are different colors but very simple. I tie up my hijab differently based on what I am wearing and sometimes I wear a hat on top of it. When I want my outfit to pop out, I tie the hijab tight to prevent it from being main element of my outfit. The person who most influenced my clothing style is without doubt my mom. From time to time, I’m inspired by her pictures from when she was young. However, I’m also inspired from models or celebrities on Instagram. Because as we are living in an interactive world, it’s now possible to know how everyone else is dressed. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/fashion/15STREET-Istanbul-5/merlin_146063211_7b15f648-b265-4313-a384-dfa38cb4f85e-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {