: None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2a078de-c50d-5e87-a9c3-a7c9a309de87', 'word_count': 1268, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2a078de-c50d-5e87-a9c3-a7c9a309de87'}, {'abstract': 'Dozens of countries still have laws against profane or impious speech, some carrying the death penalty. Such laws should be scrapped. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/13/opinion/blasphemy-pakistan-asia-bibi.html', 'snippet': 'Dozens of countries still have laws against profane or impious speech, some carrying the death penalty. Such laws should be scrapped. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is good news that Pakistan’s Supreme Court has acquitted and freed a Pakistani Christian woman who had already spent eight years on death row for blasphemy. In a 56-page ruling, the three justices said Asia Bibi, a farmworker in her early 50s, was the victim of mob justice aroused by unsubstantiated claims of what she said about the Prophet Muhammad in an exchange with women angry that she had sipped water from a cup used by Muslims.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/blasphemyWeb/merlin_146314953_83a41dbf-e63d-44b7-8f6e-cbc53e6f5da8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 374, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/blasphemyWeb/merlin_146314953_83a41dbf-e63d-44b7-8f6e-cbc53e6f5da8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 374}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/blasphemyWeb/merlin_146314953_83a41dbf-e63d-44b7-8f6e-cbc53e6f5da8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 639, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/12/opinion/blasphemyWeb/mer