raphy to Times readers for decades. As I look to reboot our travel journalism for the digital age, there are a few big themes I am thinking about, all aimed at helping our readers travel the world better, more knowledgeably and with more understanding. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/reader-center/14readers_travel/14readers_travel-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'We’re Reimagining Our Travel Journalism. Tell Us What You’d Like to See.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' Inside the Times', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Times', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-13T17:55:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Reader Center', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Virshup', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Virshup', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/937bc969-03b8-53ff-b583-aaf510a22edc', 'word_count': 620, 'uri': 'nyt://article/937bc969-03b8-53ff-b583-aaf510a22edc'}, {'abstract': 'These voters are leaving the Republican Party and we need to win them back. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/13/opinion/republicans-suburban-voters-2020.html', 'snippet': 'These voters are leaving the Republican Party and we need to win them back. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'An election provides a certain definitiveness for political candidates, win or lose. I know from experience, having lived through both the ups and the downs. For political parties, elections also provide a chance to reflect, learn and move forward with the business of attracting more voters next time. Or at least they should. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/13/autossell/13CANTOR/merlin_146425449_041de51c-da56-4401-8add-7ad70c16fe5b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 385, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/13/autossell/13CANTOR/merlin_146425449_041de51c-da56-4401-8add-7ad70c16fe5b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlarge