: None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c1200a7f-ec30-5f2c-8f75-f76e3d079574', 'word_count': 1339, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c1200a7f-ec30-5f2c-8f75-f76e3d079574'}, {'abstract': 'Representative-elect Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez joined activists in a protest in Representative Nancy Pelosi’s office, putting leaders on notice that the new House may be divided.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/13/us/politics/house-democrats-freshmen.html', 'snippet': 'Representative-elect Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez joined activists in a protest in Representative Nancy Pelosi’s office, putting leaders on notice that the new House may be divided.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Freshman orientation for new members of Congress had barely begun when Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez, the 29-year-old darling of the progressive left and newly elected congresswoman from New York, visited Nancy Pelosi’s office for the first time. She was not there to meet the House Democratic leader.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Left-Flank Protest on Day 1 Signals a Democratic House Divided', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Divisions on Day One: Party’s Progressive Star Protests House Leader', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, House of Representatives', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ocasio-Cortez, Alexandria', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-14T00:37:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg and Emily Cochrane', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cochrane', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d245a14c-6d36-5d7e-acc0-ae166b5d045a', 'word_count': 1151, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d245a14c-6d36-5d7e-acc0-ae166b5d045a'}, {'abstract': 'Ms. Sinema began her political career as an antiwar activist and then transformed into a pro-business conservative Democrat who often voted alongside Republicans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/13/us/kyrsten-sinema-senate-arizona.html', 'snippet': 'Ms. Sinema began her political career as an antiwar activist and then transformed into a pro-business conservative Democrat who often voted alongside Republicans.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PHOENIX — Kyrsten Sinema’s first foray into politics ended in failure when she campaigned as an antiwar activist and finished dead last out of five candidates in a race for a seat in the Arizona Legislature.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/us/14SINEMA-1-print/merlin_146791557_66598f10-e084-40b8-9583-41ace45e4095-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/14/us/14SINEMA-1-print/merlin_146791557_66598f10-e084-40b8-9583-41ace45e4095-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/us/14SINEMA-1-p