yalty program called Uber Rewards for its customers on Wednesday.  Lyft, its biggest competitor, announced earlier this week that it would start its own loyalty program in December. The programs come at a time when a growing number of ride-hailing apps, which also include  Via and Gett, are fiercely battling for business.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1057, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1057}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 582, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1163, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/travel/18uber1/18uber1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Uber and Lyft Announce Rewards Programs ', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Uber