all the cars and trucks on the road. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/14/climate/climate-change-natural-solutions.html', 'snippet': 'A new study found that the United States could store enough carbon in natural landscapes to offset all the cars and trucks on the road. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON —\xa0When people think of potential solutions to global warming, they tend to visualize technologies like solar panels or electric cars. A new study published on Wednesday, however, found that better management of forests, grasslands and soils in the United States could offset as much as 21 percent of the country’s annual greenhouse gas emissions.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/climate/15CLI-NATURALSOLUTIONS-print/merlin_140627268_2780cd27-138a-499f-822b-5d2892f4bafb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/15/climate/15CLI-NATURALSOLUTIONS-print/merlin_140627268_2780cd27-138a-499f-822b-5d2892f4bafb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/climate/15CLI-NATURALSOLUTIONS-print/merlin_140627268_2780cd27-138a-499f-822b-5d2892f4bafb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/climate/15CLI-NATURALSOLUTIONS-print/merlin_140627268_2780cd27-138a-499f-822b-5d2892f4bafb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/15/climate/15CLI-NATURALSO