er.html', 'snippet': 'How do you view death? Bitterly and fearfully? Or does it encourage you to make the most of the time you have on earth?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Bhutanese folklore says that to be happy, one ought to contemplate death five times a day. What do you think about that?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/merlin_142478745_bb8e08c4-c4e3-4c9f-a6ec-996b4647bde7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/merlin_142478745_bb8e08c4-c4e3-4c9f-a6ec-996b4647bde7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/merlin_142478745_bb8e08c4-c4e3-4c9f-a6ec-996b4647bde7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/merlin_142478745_bb8e08c4-c4e3-4c9f-a6ec-996b4647bde7-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/18bigideasarieff-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/18bigideasarieff-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/08/18/opinion/18bigideasarieff-01/18bigideasarieff-01-thumbLarge.jpg'