m collaboration.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/15/opinion/killer-robots-ai-humans.html', 'snippet': 'We should be thinking more about how much A.I. has changed our lives already, and the future of human-algorithm collaboration.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When it comes to the future of artificial intelligence, we seem to be stuck in a loop. We tell the same stories about A.I. over and over again: society is destroyed (the “Terminator” movies), the machines emulate and replace us (“Ex Machina”), the machines become gods pulling the strings (“The Matrix”). This is a dangerous way to think about A.I., because the stories we tell influence the decisions we make about how such systems should operate. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/merlin_143401536_149f2bfe-685d-4189-ae95-ffa705fd8026-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/merlin_143401536_149f2bfe-685d-4189-ae95-ffa705fd8026-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/merlin_143401536_149f2bfe-685d-4189-ae95-ffa705fd8026-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/merlin_143401536_149f2bfe-685d-4189-ae95-ffa705fd8026-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/15FINN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/15FINN-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/17/opinion/15FINN/15FINN-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Smarter Way to Think About Intelligent Machines', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Don’t Fear the Killer Robots', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Artificial Intelligence', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'ARIZONA STATE UNIVERSITY', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-15T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ed Finn', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ed', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Finn', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0683d509-26c8-5d54-9df3-416d1709eef6', 'word_count': 1247, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0683d509-26c8-5d54-9df3-416d1709eef6'}, {'abstract': 'What was once a Democratic pipe dream is now a real possibility. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/15/opinion/texas-trump-blue-red-beto.html', 'snippet': 'What was once a Democratic pipe dream is now a real possibility. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Enthusiastic Democrats can often be heard talking about how Texas is turning purple and maybe even blue. Professional strategists have mostly scoffed at this idea — after all, Donald Trump won Texas by more than 800,000 votes in 2016. But if President Trump decides to seek a second term — and he has said many times that he intends to — he can no longer count on winning Texas’s 38 Electoral College votes.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/merlin_146421114_2cf47ab1-4c91-4280-9e9d-bdd4b9033c19-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/merlin_146421114_2cf47ab1-4c91-4280-9e9d-bdd4b9033c19-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/merlin_146421114_2cf47ab1-4c91-4280-9e9d-bdd4b9033c19-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/merlin_146421114_2cf47ab1-4c91-4280-9e9d-bdd4b9033c19-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/14edsall1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/14edsall1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/14/opinion/14edsall1/14edsall1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Long as Trump Is President, Blue Texas Could Actually Happen', 'kicker': Non