on of the landmark musical from 1975 is a pleasure, an education and a problem.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/15/theater/a-chorus-line-review.html', 'snippet': 'City Center’s production of the landmark musical from 1975 is a pleasure, an education and a problem.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When “A Chorus Line” opened on Broadway in 1975 — having step-ball-changed its way uptown from the New York Shakespeare Festival — it was the livingest thing in a dead zone. Over its 15-year run, its youthful vigor helped resuscitate the moribund theater district, and musical theater in general.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/16/arts/16chorusline-1/merlin_146841519_4f084044-2f26-4ca7-8df4-fcf1cd72e8c8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/16/arts/16chorusline-1/merlin_146841519_4f084044-2f26-4ca7-8df4-fcf1cd72e8c8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/16/arts/16chorusline-1/merlin_146841519_4f084044-2f26-4ca7-8df4-fcf1cd72e8c8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 513, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/16/arts/16chorusline-1/merlin_146841519_4f084044-2f26-4ca7-8df4-fcf1cd72e8c8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1025, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/16/arts/16chorusline-1/16chorusline-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': '