 subjects, from historical fiction out of Italy (“The Novel of Ferrara”) to essays about Asian-American identity and other topics (“The Souls of Yellow Folk”) to the fraught evolution of particularly American catchphrases (“Behold, America”) to the book you were probably going to buy anyway, if only to keep up with your neighbors (Michelle Obama’s memoir, “Becoming”). If you have time left over, you can turn back to last week’s recommendations for a little hair of the dog.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 225, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed-covers-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 225}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed-covers-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 384, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed-covers-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 1171, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed-covers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed-covers-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/books/review/18ed-covers/18ed