 Stanley B. Greenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stanley', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/37e50567-864b-5146-98d4-12362cf5a773', 'word_count': 1361, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37e50567-864b-5146-98d4-12362cf5a773'}, {'abstract': 'Sure, telling dinner guests what you’re thankful for can feel contrived. Do it anyway. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/17/opinion/sunday/thanksgiving-gratitude-thanks.html', 'snippet': 'Sure, telling dinner guests what you’re thankful for can feel contrived. Do it anyway. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In our house, it has always been the most dreaded part of Thanksgiving. More painful than hand-scrubbing the casserole pan. More excruciating than listening to our libertarian cousin. I speak of the custom of forced gratitude — of going around the table and telling everyone what we’re thankful for.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/opinion/sunday/18jacobs-top/18jacobs-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 509, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/18/opinion/sunday/18jacobs-top/18jacobs-top-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 509}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/opinion/sunday/18jacobs-top/18jacobs-top-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 868, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/opinion/sunday/18jacobs-top/18jacobs-top-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1736, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capt