/davids-bridal-bankruptcy.html', 'snippet': 'The wedding retailer, the country’s largest, said its more than 300 stores will remain open as it seeks to shed over $400 million in debt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'David’s Bridal, the largest wedding retailer in the country, filed for Chapter 11 bankruptcy protection on Monday as it tries to shed more than $400 million in debt and adjust to new rivals, but it promised brides that no one would lose their gowns.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/business/20DAVIDS/merlin_147084309_c85fa9a9-9a0e-4ed6-83fe-bac2a19c4357-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'David’s Bridal Files for Bankruptcy, but Brides Will Get Their Dresses', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'David’s Bridal Files for Bankruptcy Protection', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "David's Bridal Inc", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shopping and Retail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bankruptcies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dresses', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Clayton Dubilier & Rice', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-19T21:20:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tiffany Hsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tiffany', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1577e0ff-5259-55d9-a2ee-e8f5f54d5eca', 'word_count': 478, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1577e0ff-5259-55d9-a2ee-e8f5f54d5eca'}, {'abstract': 'Made in Tennessee, Tigertail — from the German mustard company Develey — boasts classic flavors, as well as inventive ones.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/19/dining/tigertail-mustard-develey.html', 'snippet': 'Made in Tennessee, Tigertail — from the German mustard company Develey — boasts classic flavors, as well as inventive ones.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When Develey — a German mustard company founded near Munich in 1845 — sought a location in the United States, it landed in Dyersburg, Tenn., north of Memphis. The plant, its 17th, opened in 2016, and this year, itsTigertail brand of small-batch mustards became available nationwide online. The line includes the Classic, a basic yellow mustard that comes in squeeze bottles and handy tubes and is a tad less forceful and vinegary than your typical Dijon style (which the company also makes). They have a host of other flavors like Sriracha and peppercorn.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner3/21burner3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'German Mustards With an American Accent', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Squeeze: German Mustards  With an American Accent', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mustard', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Dyersburg (Tenn)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Develey Mustard & Condiment Corp', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-19T21:21:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a1aa5181-23f4-5a4d-b6c9-334942f94788', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a1aa5181-23f4-5a4d-b6c9-334942f94788'}, {'abstract': 'The new subscription box includes a badge each month, so your young cook can track his progress on his apron.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/19/dining/raddish-cooking-subscription-box.html', 'snippet': 'The new subscription box includes a badge each month, so your young cook can track his progress on his apron.', 'lead_paragraph': 'November’s recipes were corn pudding, cranberry crostini and maple pumpkin pie. In December, subscribers to Raddish, a monthly cooking instruction kit designed for children 4 to 14, can make rosemary focaccia, minestrone soup and hot cocoa cupcakes. The step-by-step recipes are simple but intelligent (adult novices, take note). The focaccia, for example, is a yeasted bread. Background material on ingredients provides teachable moments; November’s box covered Native American lore about corn, cranberries and pumpkin. An apron comes with a 12-month subscription. A utensil and a completion patch are included in each box.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 728, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 728}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 844, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1688, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21burner2/21burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Raddish Brings Cooking Lessons to Your Child’s Mailbox', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Practice: An Instruction Kit Aimed at Young Cooks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'key