word_count': 714, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7b9e2b9d-249f-50a3-b330-49ca1f035934'}, {'abstract': 'Take a step back after knocking. Keep your hands out of your pockets. Never argue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/20/magazine/how-to-go-door-to-door.html', 'snippet': 'Take a step back after knocking. Keep your hands out of your pockets. Never argue.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You never know who’s behind that door,” says Angel Darcourt, who has knocked on many thousands of doors in the six years she has worked as a canvasser for Working America, the community-organizing arm of the A.F.L.-C.I.O., whose unions represent some 12.5 million workers. She has knocked for issues, politicians and donations in the rain, snow and triple-digit heat in Florida, Minnesota, California, Illinois, Missouri, Michigan and West Virginia. Don’t prejudge people based on the car they drive, their Rottweiler, their race, gender, religion or age. If a child answers the door, don’t introduce yourself; just ask for a grown-up.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/magazine/18mag-tip-1/18mag-tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/18/magazine/18mag-tip-1/18mag-tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 790}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/magazine/18mag-tip-1/18mag-tip-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 778, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/18/magazine/18mag-tip-1/18mag-tip-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2022, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 's