-estate-transactions.html', 'snippet': 'Recent commercial real estate transactions in New York City.', 'lead_paragraph': '$18.25 MILLION', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1536, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/realestate/commercial/21transFor-Sale/21transFor-Sale--thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Recent Commercial Real Estate Transactions', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Transactions', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate (Commercial)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Forest Hills (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Garment District (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-20T14:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'subsection_name': 'Commercial Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosalie R. Radomsky', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosalie', 'middlename': 'R.', 'lastname': 'Radomsky', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a599953a-2778-5a10-9039-331472aa77b2', 'word_count': 377, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a599953a-2778-5a10-9039-331472aa77b2'}, {'abstract': 'Two creative people in two different fields in one wide-ranging conversation. This time: the singer and the director.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/20/t-magazine/rufus-wainwright-ivo-van-hove-conversation.html', 'snippet': 'Two creative people in two different fields in one wide-ranging conversation. This time: the singer and the director.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does the Belgian dramatist Ivo van Hove have in common with the American-Canadian singer Rufus Wainwright? For one, they’re both artists whose gay identity is neither incidental to their work nor all-consuming. For another, they are both tireless artistic explorers, catholic in the extreme. Wainwright, son of the ’70s singer-songwriters Loudon Wainwright III and Kate McGarrigle, fused indie folk and soft glam into a series of highly personal albums, beginning with his eponymous debut in 1998 and continuing through his pair of dynamic 2003-4 “Want” albums. Then he decided to write operas — the second, “Hadrian,” with a libretto by Daniel MacIvor, premiered in Toronto in October — and to compose music for the renowned American experimental theater director Robert Wilson’s 2009 staging of Shakespeare’s sonnets in Berlin. These works brought him into the creative orbit of the Amsterdam-based van Hove, whose freewheeling multimedia adaptations pay equal homage to avant-garde performance pioneers like Wilson and august playwrights like Arthur Miller, whose “The Crucible” and “A View From the Bridge” he reimagined earlier this decade. (His theater company, Internationaal Theater Amsterdam, recently premiered “A Little Life,” adapted from the novel written by T’s editor in chief, Hanya Yanagihara.) Wainwright and van Hove met up one October night in a Japanese restaurant in downtown New York; van Hove, 60, had just finished a day of rehearsals for the Broadway adaptation of Sidney Lumet’s prescient 1976 media satire, “Network” (opening Dec. 6), which he is directing and which stars Bryan Cranston. Wainwright, 45, had just flown in from his home in Los Angeles, the day after debuting his tense, beautiful and political new single, “Sword of Damocles,” as he prepares to go on tour. They were coming from disparate places, running on different clocks, but immediately opened up about that which matters most to them: politics, coming out, the multiplicity of the self — and the benefits of boarding school. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/t-magazine/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO/20tmag-conversation-slide-ATTO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rufus Wainwright and Ivo van Hove Talk Politics, Coming Out and Boarding School', 'kicker': 'Admiration Society', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'van Hove, Ivo', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wainwright, Rufus', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-20T14:30:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Boris Kachka', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Boris', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kachka', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8fbc3e50-3d1a-5809-b86b-c63847bcd4ba', 'word_count': 2026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8fbc3e50-3d1a-5809-b86b-c63847bcd4ba'}, {'abstract': 'Black Friday and Cyber Monday may be known for hot gadgets and electronics, but there are great deals on other things, too. Here are a few to watch out for.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/20/smarter-living/wirecutter/how-to-get-the-most-out-of-black-friday-even-if-youre-not-into-tech.html', 'snippet': 'Black Friday and Cyber Monday may be known for hot gadgets and electronics, but there are great deals on other things, too. Here are a few to watch out for.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Whether you’re looking to upgrade your TV or your cutting board, there’s a strong chance you’ll get the opportunity to do so this Black Friday. At Wirecutter, we watch for discounts on great gear every day, so we can help you decide whether those deals are worth taking advantage of.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/smarter-living/wc-blackfriday-slide-LF35/wc-blackfriday-slide-LF35-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/20/smarter-living/wc-blackfriday-slide-LF35/wc-blackfriday-slide-LF35-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/smarter-living/wc-blackfriday-slide-LF35/wc-blackfriday-slide-LF35-jumbo.jpg', 'he