-b8b5-67ef89d2641b'}, {'abstract': 'November is the high-stakes Super Bowl for editors at food magazines. Here’s how they strategize their cover images.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/20/dining/thanksgiving-magazine-cover.html', 'snippet': 'November is the high-stakes Super Bowl for editors at food magazines. Here’s how they strategize their cover images.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No matter how colorful they are, or how perfectly crimped their crusts, pies are unreliable cover stars. So are heaps of mashed potatoes, even when melted butter, the color of pure sunlight, pools in their dimples. As a general rule, November’s food magazines lead with the birds.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 853, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 853}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 721, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1441, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21covers9/21covers9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Bird Rules the Thanksgiving Magazine Cover', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Cover Competition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Turkeys', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Magazines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bon Appetit (Magazine)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cooking Light', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food & Wine', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Food Network Magazine', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Martha Stewart Living Omnimedia Inc', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Real Simple', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ray, Rachael', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-20T17:13:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tejal Rao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tejal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0a099466-03df-5da9-af6a-19ee1f0c1638', 'word_count': 1546, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0a099466-03df-5da9-af6a-19ee1f0c1638'}, {'abstract': 'Unconventional Thai in Hell’s Kitchen, a tribute to Brigitte Bardot and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/20/dining/nyc-restaurant-news.html', 'snippet': 'Unconventional Thai in Hell’s Kitchen, a tribute to Brigitte Bardot and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Marc Glosserman, who brought his Texas roots to New York and founded the various Hill Country restaurants, has turned what was his barbecue place in Brooklyn into a spacious food hall with an outdoor vibe. “I want it to be like a gathering of food trucks,” he said. Here, there aren’t trucks, but rough-hewed stalls to provide sustenance from morning (coffee and Du’s Donuts) until night (Van Leeuwen ice cream and cocktails). Fried chicken, including some new sandwiches, will be on offer, along with baby back ribs and other barbecue. And there’s Austino’s, for square pizza Texas-style; Bluebonnets, serving vegetable-forward sandwiches and salads; and Nickie’s Tex-Mex specialties, including tamales, nachos and burgers with salsa. Libations are soft, hard and in-between. On the second floor, a sprawling new version of Hank’s Saloon, a venerable dive bar that is closing in Boerum Hill, will be installed by early next year. (Opens Monday) ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21OFF2/merlin_146929110_feaff194-c4f4-4a61-bf09-0073ecc562f1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21OFF2/merlin_146929110_feaff194-c4f4-4a61-bf09-0073ecc562f1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21OFF2/merlin_146929110_feaff194-c4f4-4a61-bf09-0073ecc562f1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21