20SCI-QUESTIONS-INTERSTELLAR-hp/20SCI-QUESTIONS-INTERSTELLAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/20/science/20SCI-QUESTIONS-INTERSTELLAR-hp/20SCI-QUESTIONS-INTERSTELLAR-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/20/science/20SCI-QUESTIONS-INTERSTELLAR-hp/20SCI-QUESTIONS-INTERSTELLAR-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Scientific Mysteries Do You Want Solved?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-11-21T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Natalie Proulx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Natalie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Proulx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6e4c39e0-ec81-5d33-9b97-5a20b3371e5c', 'word_count': 1056, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6e4c39e0-ec81-5d33-9b97-5a20b3371e5c'}, {'abstract': 'It’s a monument to its own fraudulence — and the irrepressible nature of truth.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/21/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-plymouth-rock.html', 'snippet': 'It’s a monument to its own fraudulence — and the irrepressible nature of truth.', 'lead_paragraph': 'If you are an American over the age of 6, chances are you have a mental image of that moment, in December of 1620, when the Pilgrims stepped ashore in Plymouth: a gray sky, a craggy coast and bone-chilling waters holding the Mayflower in the distance as a huddle of God-fearing voyagers, all with solemn expressions and oversize cockel hats, lasso their sloop to a rock. You can picture it because, every November, the story of the Pilgrims gets puréed with yams and spoon-fed to just about every kindergartner in the country. This is, like most Americans, how I first learned about Plymouth Rock.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 437, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 437}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1491, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-lor-1/25mag-lor-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Letter of Recommendation: Plymouth Rock', 'kicker': 'Letter of Recommendation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Plymouth Rock', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pilgrims (Plymouth, Mass)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Monuments and Memorials (Structures)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Plymouth (Mass)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-21T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Max Rubin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Max', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rubin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b21b172e-965e-5419-8a8f-c6dac88de86f', 'word_count': 942, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b21b172e-965e-5419-8a8f-c6dac88de86f'}, {'abstract': 'Among young women in Troy, N.Y., the photographer Brenda Ann Kenneally captures a spiral of aimlessness and trouble.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/21/magazine/a-chronicle-of-life-and-pain-in-upstate-new-york.html', 'snippet': 'Among young women in Troy, N.Y., the photographer Brenda Ann Kenneally captures a spiral of aimlessness and trouble.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Brenda Ann Kenneally’s masterful new photo book, “Upstate Girls: Unraveling Collar City,” is a deep study of a group of girls from two or three extended families in Troy, N.Y. Most of them live in the same neighborhood, even on the same block. “Upstate Girls” begins in 2004, when Kenneally is drawn to the story of 14-year-old Kayla, who is pregnant. Kayla’s partner is Sabrina, also 14. The baby daddy is Sabrina’s cousin Joshua, and the pregnancy is a result of a casual encounter between Kayla and Joshua while Kayla and Sabrina were on the outs. But with the baby almost due and Joshua in prison, Kayla and Sabrina are back together, determined to be co-parents.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-articleLarge.png', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-jumbo.png', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/magazine/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL/25mag-onphoto-slide-J3PL-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chronicle of Life and Pain in Upstate New York', 'kicker': 'On Photography', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chronicle of Life and Pain in Upstate New York', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kenneally, Brenda Ann', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York State', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-21T10:00:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teju Cole', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teju', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cole', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c779cd6-f13f-56ac-9631-200816b89449', 'word_count': 1497, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c779cd6-f13f-56ac-9631-200816b89449'}, {'abstract': 'Phoebe Philo has left the house, but fans are still chasing the designer’s greatest hits. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/21/fashion/celine-phoebe-philo.html', 'snippet': 'Phoebe Philo has left the house, but fans are still chasing the designer’s greatest hits. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gabrielle Boucinha, a freelance graphic designer, introduced her Instagram account in the wake of Phoebe Philo’s much lamented exit from Celine. Her feed, @oldceline, a compilation of images dating from Ms. Philo’s decade-long tenure at the luxury house, has drawn an ardent following, swelling from a few hundred in September, when Hedi Slimane was set to replace Ms. Philo as creative director, to a current 143,000. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/fashion/22CELINE10/merlin_147131757_6b433785-2a95-470a-b82f-e65a33cacc00-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xl