stract': 'Wait, wait, shiver, delight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/21/nyregion/for-nearly-100-years-the-macys-parade-has-been-a-childrens-pilgrimage-of-wonder.html', 'snippet': 'Wait, wait, shiver, delight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It is a hard rite to explain: To commemorate the multicultural harvest feast of 1621 at Plymouth Rock, about three million New Yorkers and visitors annually station themselves on freezing late-November streets to watch giant inflatable branded cartoon characters, all promoting a department store that filed for bankruptcy protection more than 25 years ago. Something like that. More than 40 million people watch it on television. Even compared to eating turkey, a dish that few people truly make well, the Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade, now in its 92nd year, is a bit of a head-scratcher.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1348, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/nyregion/21paradepics-ast-10/21paradepics-ast-10-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'For Nearly 100 Years, Macy’s Thanksgiving Day Parade Has Been a Children’s Pilgrimage of Wonder', 'kicker': 'Past Tense', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Wait, Shiver, Delight: A Children’s Pilgrimage of Wonder', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Thanksgiving Day', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parades', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black Friday and Cyber Monday (Shopping)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Macy's Inc", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'White, E B', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-21T10:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Leland', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leland', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/806455fd-1241-53f5-8825-07a7cc18e32f', 'word_count': 426, 'uri': 'nyt://article/806455fd-1241-53f5-8825-07a7cc18e32f'}, {'abstract': 'The annual purgatory we endure for family and friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/21/travel/holiday-travel-delay-pictures-history.html', 'snippet': 'The annual purgatory we endure for family and friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Late one night, in the early part of each November, there occurs an annual phantom hour. It creeps into the deserted region from 1 to 2 in the morning, and then vanishes, leaving everything changed. From this moment, 50 degrees is warm, not cold. Sunsets are confined to the realm of memory. Conclaves of blood-red cardinals congregate on decorative hand towels and doormats, even in trees. The American holiday season (which ends firmly on Jan. 2, but can be safely assumed to be revving up or underway on all other dates) escalates to Defcon 1, at which level it will remain for several dazzling weeks.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 378, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 378}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 645, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1290, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25waiting-ast3-print4/21waiting-ast3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Holiday Travel Has Been Terrible for at Least 50 Years. We Have the Pictures to Prove It.', 'kicker': 'Past Tense', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Home for the Holidays? Not So Fast, Pilgrims', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holidays and Special Occasions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-21T10:00:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Caity Weaver', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Caity', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weaver', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a2963f7d-5057-58c6-be72-01cedfcb1fe6', 'word_count': 528, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a2963f7d-5057-58c6-be72-01cedfcb1fe6'}, {'abstract': 'A small enclave with a big personality, the riverside neighborhood is a “live-and-let-live kind of place.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/21/realestate/snedens-landing-palisades-ny-wildflowers-artists-and-celebrities.html', 'snippet': 'A small enclave with a big personality, the riverside neighborhood is a “live-and-let-live kind of place.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1937, the writer E.B. White described Snedens Landing as “steeped in Hudson Valley mists and memories — people make their own wine, stamp out their own copperhead snakes, go picking Dutchman’s breeches in the spring. On summer evenings, you can hear the trains across the river, grumbling. There is a good deal of talk about shad.”', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS/25LIVINGIN-PALISADES-slide-NKUS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, '