rmation of a neighborhood. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/realestate/what-amazon-means-for-long-island-city.html', 'snippet': 'Interest in real estate open houses has already spiked, and prices will likely rise. Here’s a in depth look at the transformation of a neighborhood. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hopes are high in Long Island City that Amazon’s plan to open a new headquarters there will bring tens of thousands more residents to a Queens neighborhood that was once heavily industrial but now has a mix of rowhouses, shiny towers, and a slowly growing collection of residential staples like grocery stores and pharmacies.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/merlin_147101733_3909bff7-b61f-4e15-8370-a4feee3e2f64-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/merlin_147101733_3909bff7-b61f-4e15-8370-a4feee3e2f64-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/merlin_147101733_3909bff7-b61f-4e15-8370-a4feee3e2f64-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/merlin_147101733_3909bff7-b61f-4e15-8370-a4feee3e2f64-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/25LIC6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/25LIC6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/realestate/25LIC6/25LIC6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What Amazon Means for Long Island City', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long Island City’s Next Act', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMAZON.COM INC', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Long Island City (Queens, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Relocation of Business', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T09:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By C. J. Hughes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'C.', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'Hughes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/96101329-2596-5d74-bb09-7e11410c379d', 'word_count': 1757, 'uri': 'nyt://article/96101329-2596-5d74-bb09-7e11410c379d'}, {'abstract': 'After the wedding, he introduced me as his wife. I don’t know why this startled me so much, but each time he said it I shrunk inside. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/style/self-care/what-is-it-about-the-word-wife.html', 'snippet': 'After the wedding, he introduced me as his wife. I don’t know why this startled me so much, but each time he said it I shrunk inside. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'My mother, in an effort to keep me humble and rooted, likes to remind me of embarrassing facts from my childhood. Her favorite one lately: I marched up and down the hallway belting out “Here Comes the Bride” with a sheer beige curtain over my head as a veil. If anyone asked me what I wanted to be when I grew up, my 5-year-old voice proudly said, “a bride.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 217, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 217}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 371, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/style/22Rites-wife-1/22Rites-wife-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How I Came to Hate the Word ‘Wife’', 'kicker': 'Rites of passage', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weddings and Engagements', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dating and Relationships', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Divorce, Separations and Annulments', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'subsection_name': 'Self-Care', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marcia Walker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marcia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Walker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9764a123-8223-5910-af8a-3b7d48027f98', 'word_count': 1512, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9764a123-8223-5910-af8a-3b7d48027f98'}, {'abstract': 'Selected by Rita Dove.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/magazine/poem-only-as-the-day-is-long.html', 'snippet': 'Selected by Rita Dove.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The title poem of Dorianne Laux’s forthcoming collection is a searing eulogy, a heart-rending kaddish whose compassion is tendered with an unblinking eye. It also happens to be a sonnet, albeit unrhymed — still singing although turned on its head, with the six-line stanza followed by the octave. It’s a fitting vessel for this litany of conflicted sorrow as Laux takes us from the cellular level to the vastness of the universe, all the while gathering the devastating minutiae of a not-quite-vanished life. Selected by Rita Dove', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-poem-image