e, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/149348cb-3b01-573e-ae65-af1079d4a5f9', 'word_count': 87, 'uri': 'nyt://article/149348cb-3b01-573e-ae65-af1079d4a5f9'}, {'abstract': 'In these turbulent times, charitable clicks are a form of self-soothing as well as generosity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/style/donation-panic-giving-tuesday.html', 'snippet': 'In these turbulent times, charitable clicks are a form of self-soothing as well as generosity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Before the 2016 election, Tess Malone, 28, rarely engaged in charitable giving outside of disaster relief funds or individual GoFundMe fund-raising campaigns. But now, donating — often in the form of a late-night, anxiety-fueled frenzy — is as standard an expenditure for her as groceries and dining out.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-articleLarge.gif', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-jumbo.gif', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-superJumbo.gif', 'height': 1500, 'width': 1500, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-thumbStandard.gif', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-thumbStandard.gif', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/fashion/25PANICDONATIONS/25PANICDONATIONS-thumbLarge.gif', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Time to Make the Donates!', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For the Disaffected, It’s Better to Give Than to Concede', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gun Control', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gray Chapman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gray', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chapman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4ce3b956-8a16-5973-94f7-d310aaedb994', 'word_count': 1713, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4ce3b956-8a16-5973-94f7-d310aaedb994'}, {'abstract': 'With a bit of planning, the Eternal City can be at its most bewitching at the onset of winter.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/travel/what-to-do-in-rome-36-hours.html', 'snippet': 'With a bit of planning, the Eternal City can be at its most bewitching at the onset of winter.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For all its imperial and papal pomp and circumstance, Rome at heart is a beautiful child — raucous, dreamy, secretive, a touch spoiled, by turns exasperating and enchanting. The child is on its best behavior during “le feste” — the winter holidays. High season crowds thin, and dazzling light displays and slanting sunbeams compensate for the short days. Today’s Rome is a paradoxical place: even as many historic neighborhoods fall to mass-touristic homogeneity, outlying districts are becoming more vibrant and varied. For an authentic Roman holiday, get out of the centro storico and sample the pizza stalls of the Testaccio market and the funky wares at the nearby Porta Portese Sunday flea market, the nightclubs of San Lorenzo and Tiburtina, and neighborhood gelaterie like Neve di Latte and La Mucca Bianca. Tranquillity has never been Rome’s strong suit, but with a bit of planning (and flexibility), the Eternal City can be at its most bewitching at the onset of winter. (Though buses and trams crisscross the city, you’ll save time with two easy-to-navigate taxi apps — My Taxi and It Taxi.)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/merlin_146942058_da2b5e4d-1e29-433e-b620-45ce62e21d8e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/merlin_146942058_da2b5e4d-1e29-433e-b620-45ce62e21d8e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/merlin_146942058_da2b5e4d-1e29-433e-b620-45ce62e21d8e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/merlin_146942058_da2b5e4d-1e29-433e-b620-45ce62e21d8e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/02Hours-Rome3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/02Hours-Rome3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02Hours-Rome3/02Hours-Rome3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '36 Hours in Rome', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rome', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Travel and Vacations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Rome (Italy)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Laskin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Laskin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6fab62e8-66bd-5acf-a6f6-d566e96d7385', 'word_count': 1577, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6fab62e8-66bd-5acf-a6f6-d566e96d7385'}, {'abstract': 'It’s funny, and it’s easy. But is it O.K.?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-on-fooling-babies.html', 'snippet': 'It’s funny, and it’s easy. But is it O.K.?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Becca writes: We have a happy baby boy who is just starting to babble a little bit. He makes the sound “dada” a lot. My husband thinks it’s funny to say, “Yes, that’s your dada,” and point at whatever the baby is looking at (for example, the dog, a toy, another person). But I think this is confusing for the baby, and we should be trying to encourage him to use “dada” to mean his actual dad.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/mag-hodgman-image-articleLarge-v4.png', 'height': 369, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/mag-hodgman-image-articleLarge-v4.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 369}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/mag-hodgman-image-jumbo-v4.png', 'height': 630, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/mag-hodgman-image-superJumbo-v4.png', 'height': 1259, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/08mag-hodgman-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/08mag-hodgman-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/04/08/magazine/mag-hodgman-image/08mag-hodgman-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge John Hodgman on Fooling Babies', 'kicker': 'Judge John Hodgman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bonus Advice From Judge John Hodgman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Judge John Hodgman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Judge', 'middlename': 'John', 'lastname': 'Hodgman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c7f43c6b-0475-5c55-9c86-363d5efb8424', 'word_count': 163, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c7f43c6b-0475-5c55-9c86-363d5efb8424'}, {'abstract': 'Jho Low, the financier charged with looting billions from a Malaysian fund, had an audience in 2012 with Lloyd C. Blankfein, the chairman and chief executive of Goldman Sachs.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/business/goldman-blankfein-1mdb-malaysia.html', 'snippet': 'Jho Low, the financier charged with looting billions from a Malaysian fund, had an audience in 2012 with Lloyd C. Blankfein, the chairman and chief executive of Goldman Sachs.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One day in December 2012, a young Malaysian V.I.P. entered the gleaming headquarters of Goldman Sachs in Lower Manhattan. The man, Jho Low, a financier with close ties to Malaysia’s prime minister at the time, was there for a private meeting with one of the most powerful people on Wall Street: Goldman’s longtime chairman and chief executive, Lloyd C. Blankfein.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'ty