nd the Hooghly River, a 160-mile branch of the Ganges that runs through the city of Kolkata in West Bengal, is no different. In the late afternoon, I walked to Babu Ghat, and onto the broad concrete slipway that descended into the water, where a few moored boats bobbed slowly and men and children bathed in underclothes. ', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/travel/25Frugal-Kolkata/25Frugal-Kolkata-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Kolkata, a Love of Literature, Fried Street Food and, Mostly, Sweets', 'kicker': 'frugal traveler', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Kolkata, a Love of Literature, Fried Food and Sweets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Budget Travel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indian Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kolkata (India)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Bengal (India)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Travel', 'section_name': 'Travel', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lucas Peterson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lucas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Peterson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f555a2b-e5ad-53c5-9a17-bc7808a03a31', 'word_count': 1850, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f555a2b-e5ad-53c5-9a17-bc7808a03a31'}, {'abstract': 'They’re arguing for their place at top restaurants by imbuing classic desserts with new forms, ingredients and undeniable originality.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/t-magazine/american-pies-cakes-desserts.html', 'snippet': 'They’re arguing for their place at top restaurants by imbuing classic desserts with new forms, ingredients and undeniable originality.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PIE, NICOLE RUCKER will tell you, has its own story to tell. On the Los Angeles baker’s Instagram feed, that tale includes golden, all-butter crusts that bubble over with apricots, rhubarb, strawberries and peaches — and one that comes infused with THC. They convey bounty and comfort, as pies do, but also wanton experimentation: The weed one, topped with candied cannabis leaves from Rucker’s own garden and served at a friend’s birthday party, was a marriage between classic key lime and “all of the new products,” the chef says.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 463, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 463}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 790, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1580, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/22/t-magazine/22tmag-cake/22tmag-cake-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'As Pastry Chefs Decline in Ranks, a Revolution in Cakes and Pies', 'kicker': 'SOCIAL STUDIES', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bakeries and Baked Products', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cakes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Momofuku Milk Bar (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tosi, Christina', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Vongerichten, Jean-Georges', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rebecca Flint Marx', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rebecca', 'middlename': 'Flint', 'lastname': 'Marx', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6ca48e76-f952-572f-9423-9a3cd9804790', 'word_count': 993, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6ca48e76-f952-572f-9423-9a3cd9804790'}, {'abstract': 'A reader taught her nephew how to be smart about money when he was a teenager. Now that he’s an adult with cash and credit, he wants her to subsidize his very expensive nuptials. What?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/style/wedding-cost-money-advice.html', 'snippet': 'A reader taught her nephew how to be smart about money when he was a teenager. Now that he’s an adult with cash and credit, he wants her to subsidize his very expensive nuptials. What?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My nephew is 30. His parents died when he was 18, leaving him impoverished. Since then, I’ve provided financial guidance and emotional support. He was able to graduate from college debt free and has a good job. Against my advice, he used his savings for a down payment on a house I don’t believe he can afford. He is now planning an expensive wedding to his fiancée, who has substantial student debt. He asked if I would pay for their rehearsal dinner. I was outraged and refused! I will attend the wedding, but I don’t believe people should buy things they can’t afford. Was I wrong?', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Fancy Wedding Is Everything I Didn’t Want for You', 'kicker': 'SOCIAL Q’S', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Indebted to Whom?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-22T10:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9c930a04-78e0-5b5c-996d-156ea5947c06', 'word_count': 860, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9c930a04-78e0-5b5c-996d-156ea5947c06'}, {'abstract': 'Sign of the times? The University of Iowa, home to the famous Writers’ Workshop, now has a television-writing course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/22/books/novelists-tv-shows-series.html', 'snippet': 'Sign of the times? The University of Iowa, home to the famous Writers’ Workshop, now has a television-writing course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The borders between television and prose fiction grow ever porous. At the University of Iowa’s Writers’ Workshop — a bastion of literary purity for aspiring novelists and poets, which, not coincidentally, has been featured on the TV show “Girls” — evidence of this porousness is sometimes subtle: “It happened a few years ago,” said the workshop’s director, Lan Samantha Chang. “Everyone was suddenly using the word ‘reveal’ as a noun.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/books/review/23Alford-01/16Alford-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 356, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/23/books/review/23Alford-01/16Alford-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 356}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/books/review/23Alford-01/16Alford-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 607, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'c