d his family had to give up all its possessions for fear of contamination, after he was sickened in the assault on Sergei V. Skripal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — The British police officer who was poisoned in a nerve agent attack on a Russian former spy has said that he and his family had to abandon all their belongings because of possible contamination — not just their home and cars, but every item in them, from family mementos to their children’s toys.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/merlin_135072192_39cd9b15-32f4-488e-8f70-52512a675aed-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/merlin_135072192_39cd9b15-32f4-488e-8f70-52512a675aed-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/merlin_135072192_39cd9b15-32f4-488e-8f70-52512a675aed-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/merlin_135072192_39cd9b15-32f4-488e-8f70-52512a675aed-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/24skripal1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/24skripal1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/24/world/24skripal1/24skripal1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Lost Everything,’ Says U.K. Police Officer Poisoned in Novichok Attack', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Officer Says Family Lost Everything In Poisoning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poisoning and Poisons', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Skripal, Sergei V', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Salisbury (England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-23T12:18:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard Pérez-Peña', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pérez-Peña', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4b30ed6c-56f5-5229-a8a8-db492a0516c9', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4b30ed6c-56f5-5229-a8a8-db492a0516c9'}, {'abstract': 'Michael Cunningham, Elif Batuman and Hilton Als respond to some of the artist’s most iconic pictures ahead of an exhibition of his work at the Guggenheim.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/23/t-magazine/robert-mappelthorpe-michael-cunningham-elif-batuman-hilton-als.html', 'snippet': 'Michael Cunningham, Elif Batuman and Hilton Als respond to some of the artist’s most iconic pictures ahead of an exhibition of his work at the Guggenheim.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The photographer Robert Mapplethorpe is well known for his nudes, his portrayals of New York’s various underground worlds and his friendships with Patti Smith, Grace Jones and the bodybuilder Lisa Lyon, among others. He was also a documentarian of the quieter moments in life — two lovers sharing a simple kiss, a flower shot to resemble the human form — all of which will be on display in “Implicit Tensions: Mapplethorpe Now,” a wide-ranging, yearlong show of his work at the Guggenheim Museum in New York, beginning Jan. 25, 2019. In his photographs, you learn as much about the artist — whose death, at the age of 42 in 1989, was due to complications from AIDS — as you do his subjects. “The whole point of being an artist or making a statement is to learn about yourself,” he once said. “The photographs, I think, are less important than the life that one is leading.” We asked three writers to create short fictions based on three of his most iconic images.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1187, 'width': 1779, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-copy/23tmag-mapplethorpe-slide-102C-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trio of Short Fictions Inspired by Robert Mapplethorpe Photographs', 'kicker': 'Art Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Love (Emotion)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mapplethorpe, Robert', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'West Village (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kissing', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-23T12:35:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Cunningham, Elif Batuman and Hilton Als', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cunningham', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Elif', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Batuman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Hilton', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Als', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/11007df6-594f-5be6-a470-ad089ffbfb27', 'word_count': 2018, 'uri': 'nyt://article/11007df6-594f-5be6-a470-ad089ffbfb27'}, {'abstract': 'Loro Piana makes some of the softest textiles in the world, with help from a menagerie of sheep, goats and vicuñas.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/23/t-magazine/loro-piana-cashmere.html', 'snippet': 'Loro Piana makes some of the softest textiles in the world, with help from a menagerie of sheep, goats and vicuñas.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the mid-1980s, Pier Luigi Loro Piana, then co-president of his family’s eponymous fashion company, trekked to the frigid plateau of Inner Mongolia to visit the rarefied Capra hircus goats that produce the cashmere for the line’s clothing and accessories (Loro Piana also uses fibers from South American vicuñas and merino sheep in New Zealand and Australia). As he surveyed the herd, an idea struck: “Human baby hair is infinitely softer than an adult’s. The same is probably true of baby goats.” Thus was born baby cashmere, made from the almost-weightless inner coat of the kid, available only once in each animal’s lifetime, when they are between 3 and 8 months old. Each produces a mere single ounce of strands that average only 13.5 microns (or about 0.0005 inches) in diameter; it takes 19 ounces to make a single sweater. “Holding one of these small creatures in my arms, I had the same emotion as when I hold a baby,” Loro Piana says. “It’s a symbol of purity.” Here is the small collection of species that Loro Piana uses to create most of its textiles. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/23/t-magazine/23tmag-loropiana-slide-TFGE/23tmag-loropiana-slide-TFGE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 762, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarg