 'snippet': ' The season’s best blockbuster isn’t a TV show or movie. It’s a video game. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'After its October release, Red Dead Redemption 2 earned $725 million in just three days, giving it the highest-grossing opening weekend of any entertainment product — ever. If you’re wondering why you haven’t seen this at this box office, it’s because it’s not a movie. It’s a video game.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 336, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 336}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 573, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1074, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25SUDERMAN/25SUDERMAN-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}