ain': 'The Crash and Burn of Dolce & Gabbana', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Boycotts', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Dolce & Gabbana', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabbana, Stefano', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-23T17:27:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Vanessa Friedman and Sui-Lee Wee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Vanessa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Friedman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sui-lee', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2c19ec82-8702-52c5-b45e-ebf8a408f695', 'word_count': 1452, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2c19ec82-8702-52c5-b45e-ebf8a408f695'}, {'abstract': 'After the feast, try kale-sauce pasta, oven-steamed salmon and chicken Francese.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/23/dining/keep-it-fast-keep-it-simple.html', 'snippet': 'After the feast, try kale-sauce pasta, oven-steamed salmon and chicken Francese.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hi and welcome to Five Weeknight Dishes — though will you ever be hungry for a meal again? (Or maybe you’ve already had leftovers-laced breakfast sandwiches from this heartwarming stoner-dude story by Priya Krishna, about two brothers who run a restaurant in L.A.?) There’s something I have to tell you: I know there are a million leftovers recipes floating around out there. We’ve published them, a