iddlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/a6ecd721-b753-56c8-bc9a-8f758046bdee', 'word_count': 49, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a6ecd721-b753-56c8-bc9a-8f758046bdee'}, {'abstract': 'Medication abortions will not solve all the problems of a post-Roe world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/25/opinion/medication-abortion-roe.html', 'snippet': 'Medication abortions will not solve all the problems of a post-Roe world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As abortion rights have come under increasing attack in the United States, commentators have held up self-administered abortion pills as a backup plan for a post-Roe world. They point to the millions of pregnant women worldwide who are using pills to self-manage abortion, citing them as an example of what reproductive health care might look like should in-clinic abortions be made illegal. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25GIRARD/25GIRARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25GIRARD/25GIRARD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25GIRARD/25GIRARD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/25/opinion/25GIRARD/25GIRARD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1470, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't