essings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Preserved lemon is an essential ingredient for capturing a taste of Morocco. Not long ago, you had to make it, a time-consuming process of curing whole lemons in salt. Then whole, salted lemons became available in jars. And now New York Shuk, a small producer of North African and Middle Eastern ingredients, has introduced a smooth, jammy paste of preserved lemons that does its citric, saline work in dressings, sauces, marinades, spreads and dips.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 664, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 664}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 926, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1851, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner2/28burner2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Preserved Lemons in Paste Form', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Season: Preserved Lemons In Paste Form', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Shuk Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Citrus Fruits', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Condiments', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-26T22:21:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2223fad3-9493-5f12-af34-f1419cfc60d1', 'word_count': 110, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2223fad3-9493-5f12-af34-f1419cfc60d1'}, {'abstract': 'Grand Brulot, an aged digestif made with coffee and V.S.O.P. Cognac, is easy to savor. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/26/dining/drinks/grand-brulot-digestif.html', 'snippet': 'Grand Brulot, an aged digestif made with coffee and V.S.O.P. Cognac, is easy to savor. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Grand Brulot is a new take on the French tradition of spiking coffee with brandy as a digestif. The brandy is a V.S.O.P. Cognac from a fifth-generation estate owned by the Tardy family in the Cognac region of France. The coffee is a robusta from Ecuador, selected for its richness. The two are blended together and aged six years in oak to produce a drink that’s warming, with a hint of spice. It’s easy to savor alone or in a cocktail. The name is a play on an elaborate flamed alcoholic French coffee drink that’s popular in New Orleans.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/merlin_146988447_dd6bad03-d0da-4cc2-9e11-20caa68e4f06-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1015, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/merlin_146988447_dd6bad03-d0da-4cc2-9e11-20caa68e4f06-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1015}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/merlin_146988447_dd6bad03-d0da-4cc2-9e11-20caa68e4f06-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 606, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/merlin_146988447_dd6bad03-d0da-4cc2-9e11-20caa68e4f06-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1211, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/28burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/28burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/dining/28burner3/28burner3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Sip of French Tradition With a Hint of New Orleans', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: A Sip of French Tradition  With a Bit of New Orleans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value