rt-cooperation.html', 'snippet': 'Prosecutors said lies by Mr. Manafort, President Trump’s onetime campaign chairman, on “a variety of subject matters” relieved them of all promises they made to him in their deal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Paul Manafort, President Trump’s former campaign chairman, repeatedly lied to federal investigators in breach of a plea agreement he signed two months ago, the special counsel’s office said in a court filing late on Monday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/us/27dc-manafort-hp2/27dc-manafort-hp2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Manafort Breached Plea Deal by Repeatedly Lying, Mueller Says', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Manfort’s Lies Broke Plea Deal, Prosecutors Say', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Manafort, Paul J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mueller, Robert S III', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Plea Bargaining', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Special Prosecutors (Independent Counsel)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-27T00:02:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sharon LaFraniere', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sharon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'LaFraniere', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de3a0ccd-4260-562d-81f6-b533ea76fd3a', 'word_count': 1276, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de3a0ccd-4260-562d-81f6-b533ea76fd3a'}, {'abstract': 'Business groups and Senate Republicans are pushing to strengthen the ozone-saving Montreal Protocol. It should be an easy call for President Trump. ', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/26/opinion/trump-win-environment-montreal-protocol.html', 'snippet': 'Business groups and Senate Republicans are pushing to strengthen the ozone-saving Montreal Protocol. It should be an easy call for President Trump. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'Into the bleak landscape that is the Trump administration’s environmental record comes a new report — from the government’s own analysts — that lays out in the grimmest terms yet the consequences of continued inaction on climate change. The National Climate Assessment, issued on Friday when most Americans’ attention was on shopping, football and leftovers, predicts devastating effects from a warming planet and stands in sharp contrast to President Trump’s blithe rejection of the basic science of climate change. The report details the environmental, human and economic costs of a changing climate in the United States, including worsening drought, more vicious wildfires, wider crop failures and accelerating property damage. The impacts could reduce domestic economic activity by as much as a tenth by 2100, the report says.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 390, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 390}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 665, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1330, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/26/opinion/26enviro-edt/26enviro-edt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Trump Win for the Environment? Maybe', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Trump Win for the Planet? Maybe', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Interior Department', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Grouse (Bird)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hydrofluorocarbons', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Environmental Protection Agency', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wheeler, Andrew R', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Zinke, Ryan (1961- )', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-27T00:10:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/50760d72-3cc8-52b6-af9a-4ba8e9b98c8c', 'word_count': 1026, 'uri': 'nyt://article/50760d72-3cc8-52b6-af9a-4ba8e9b98c8c'}, {'abstract': 'The man and his twin brother had admitted in federal court that they stockpiled 32 pounds of explosives in their apartment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/26/nyregion/brothers-bomb-making-guilty.html', 'snippet': 'The man and his twin brother had admitted in federal court that they stockpiled 32 pounds of explosives in their apartment.', 'lead_paragraph': '[Update, May 22, 2019: Christian Toro, a former special needs high school teacher in the Bronx who enlisted his twin brother and two of his students in a bizarre bomb-making plot, was sentenced on Wednesday in Federal District Court in Manhattan to five and a half years in prison. Before being sentenced, Mr. Toro told Judge Richard M. Berman that his desire to manufacture explosives was brought on by severe depression and “misplaced curiosity.” Judge Berman responded, “I still don’t get why you did it.”]', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/nyregion/27terror01/27terror01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/27/nyregion/27terror01/27terror01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/nyregion/27terror01/27terror01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/nyregion/27terror01/27terror01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1452, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/27/nyregion/27terror01/27terror01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'su