, 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — When the members of Bottlesmoker, an “indietronic” band from Indonesia, landed in Vietnam last Thursday, they were looking forward to their set at Quest Festival, an annual event billed as a “wondrous, wild wonderland of nature, art and eclectic entertainment.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/merlin_147375858_02d197f9-56d1-478b-a989-2da7cf814561-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/merlin_147375858_02d197f9-56d1-478b-a989-2da7cf814561-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/merlin_147375858_02d197f9-56d1-478b-a989-2da7cf814561-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/merlin_147375858_02d197f9-56d1-478b-a989-2da7cf814561-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/28asiaconcerts-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/28asiaconcerts-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/world/02asiaconcerts/28asiaconcerts-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Music Festivals Are Gaining Popularity in Asia. Just Not With Officials.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Music Festivals Draw Fans, and Resistance, in Asia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Festivals', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-27T09:27:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mike Ives', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ives', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a09e1f9c-44a5-553a-9a0c-c4416300ab5d', 'word_count': 1066, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a09e1f9c-44a5-553a-9a0c-c4416300ab5d'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to tell an aging parent your brother is not his son and taking out a student loan to help your sibling.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/27/magazine/do-i-tell-my-father-that-my-brother-might-not-be-his-son.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether to tell an aging parent your brother is not his son and taking out a student loan to help your sibling.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am the executor of my father’s will. He is 82 years old and frail, and lately I have been troubled by a question. My brother may not be his child, and my mother and siblings all know this (including the brother in question), but my father does not. My parents are divorced and not on good terms. My mother is fairly sure that my brother is not my father’s child, but a DNA test would have to be done to be certain. If my brother is not my father’s child, does my dad deserve to know this before he dies? Name Withheld', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1400, 'width': 1400, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/10/07/magazine/02mag-ethicist-image1/02mag-ethicist-image1-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 's