 learn anything from listening to the tape of the journalist’s killing because he does not speak Arabic.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — John R. Bolton, President Trump’s national security adviser, defended on Tuesday the fact that neither Mr. Trump nor top national security officials had listened to audio of the killing of the Saudi journalist Jamal Khashoggi, saying that they did not speak Arabic and would not be able to understand what was on the tape.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '‘Why Do You Think I Should?’: Bolton Defends Not Listening to Khashoggi Tape', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bolton Balks At Questions About Tape', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Central Intelligence Agency', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Group of Twenty', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolton, John R', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Haspel, Gina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khashoggi, Jamal', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-27T21:50:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Rogers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rogers', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b38ed408-d39b-57f4-998c-3b95b3792fda', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b38ed408-d39b-57f4-998c-3b95b3792fda'}, {'abstract': 'The number of undocumented immigrants in the United States has dropp