major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kitchen, The (Manhattan, NY, Performance Space)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': "O'Grady, Lorraine (1934- )", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Gray, Alexander, Associates (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Faustine, Nona', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Higher Pictures (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-28T15:08:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b368344f-83ed-5b35-9582-97898adec700', 'word_count': 722, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b368344f-83ed-5b35-9582-97898adec700'}, {'abstract': 'If you have leftover stock on hand, make gumbo. Or prepare for Hanukkah and with a Melissa Clark recipe for olive oil and sea salt brownies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/28/dining/what-to-cook-today.html', 'snippet': 'If you have leftover stock on hand, make gumbo. Or prepare for Hanukkah and with a Melissa Clark recipe for olive oil and sea salt brownies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. I made enough turkey stock this year that I could freeze a few quarts for use this winter. The rest I used to make gumbo, employing the no-recipe technique I champion each Wednesday in this space. And if like many Americans you currently have turkey stock — or leftover chicken stock — on hand in your refrigerator or freezer, you might join me in making the dish tonight or some day soon. You will not regret it.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/21/dining/21apperex1/merlin_147045984_d26bcb86-12e7-43dd-b807-1b8e16c1e051-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subTyp