 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Private and Sectarian Schools', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brown v Board of Education (Supreme Court Decision)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Espy, Mike', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hyde-Smith, Cindy', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-28T17:47:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Noliwe Rooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Noliwe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f5b9e789-adde-56b8-94e8-320f16dd73a9', 'word_count': 1328, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f5b9e789-adde-56b8-94e8-320f16dd73a9'}, {'abstract': 'The 22-year-old singer and songwriter’s second album, “The Pains of Growing,” doubles down on both awkwardness and sincerity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/28/arts/music/alessia-cara-the-pains-of-growing-review.html', 'snippet': 'The 22-year-old singer and songwriter’s second album, “The Pains of Growing,” doubles down on both awkwardness and sincerity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Artfully awkward sincerity defined the Canadian singer and songwriter Alessia Cara on her 2015 debut album, “Know-It-All.” In one of its hits, “Here,” she sang about feeling antisocial and alienated at a loud party. And in a song that became an anthem, “Scars to Your Beautiful,” she decried superficial ideas of beauty, vowing, “To all the girls that’s hurting, let me be your mirror.” She went on to collaborate with the rapper Logic on the anti-suicide song “1-800-273-8255,” and sang an uplifting Lin-Manuel Miranda song, “How Far I’ll Go,” for the Disney movie “Moana.” She was named best new artist — a few years late — at the 2018 Grammy Awards.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/merlin_147409080_776a56ed-9fbb-48f0-b73b-eb79b80c4e46-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 406, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/merlin_147409080_776a56ed-9fbb-48f0-b73b-eb79b80c4e46-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 406}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/merlin_147409080_776a56ed-9fbb-48f0-b73b-eb79b80c4e46-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 693, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/merlin_147409080_776a56ed-9fbb-48f0-b73b-eb79b80c4e46-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1386, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/29album-alessia2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/29album-alessia2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/29/arts/29album-alessia2/29album-alessia2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Alessia Cara: Young, Gifted and Bummed Out', 'kicker': 'Album Review', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Young, Talented and Bummed Out', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cara, Alessia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Pains of Growing (Album)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-28T18:22:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Pareles', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pareles', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/55dc9a29-e837-5a92-a643-93858a781d7c', 'word_count': 565, 'uri': 'nyt://article/55dc9a29-e837-5a92-a643-93858a781d7c'}, {'abstract': 'After three weeks of draws failed to produce a winner, the players settled the title in rapid chess, with Carlsen retaining his title.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/28/sports/magnus-carlsen-fabiano-caruana-world-chess-championship.html', 'snippet': 'After three weeks of draws failed to produce a winner, the players settled the title in rapid chess, with Carlsen retaining his title.', 'lead_paragraph': 'After three weeks, 12 straight draws and a day of tiebreakers, Norway’s Magnus Carlsen finally retained the world chess championship in London on Wednesday with a victory against Fabiano Caruana, his American challenger.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/29/sports/29chess2/merlin_147428502_dccd2c25-1efe-49f1-a99e-69a36d44148e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'l