article/3adf93e7-9f98-5f0a-b6cf-e4157f0a932b', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3adf93e7-9f98-5f0a-b6cf-e4157f0a932b'}, {'abstract': 'Rice — left to rest overnight — is mixed with a brown-butter-squash purée to create a dish that is as satisfying at dinner as it is at breakfast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/29/magazine/porridge-brown-butter-squash-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Rice — left to rest overnight — is mixed with a brown-butter-squash purée to create a dish that is as satisfying at dinner as it is at breakfast.', 'lead_paragraph': '“How much time do you have?” Minh Phan wanted to know, when I showed up at her restaurant in Los Angeles after hours. I was hoping to learn how she cooked the delicious rice I ate there about a week before. It was covered with curls of see-through pickles and little scoops of sticky, savory jams, and many kinds of herbs. The grains of rice were whole and tender — soft but not soupy. How much time could we possibly need, I wondered, to boil some rice until it was tender?', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 452, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 452}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 771, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1541, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Eat-image1/02mag-Eat-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Not Your Dickensian Bowl of Porridge', 'kicker': 'Eat', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Not Your Dickensian Bowl of Porridge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rice', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnamese Food (Cuisine)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-29T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tejal Rao', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tejal', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rao', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/41803b8b-5b1a-5e60-bd01-2bd98508d3ec', 'word_count': 890, 'uri': 'nyt://article/41803b8b-5b1a-5e60-bd01-2bd98508d3ec'}, {'abstract': 'Her doctors thought the young woman had a virus commonly seen in children. But when she only got worse, one doctor looked elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/29/magazine/a-rash-on-her-palms-and-the-bottoms-of-her-feet-was-the-clue-that-turned-the-case.html', 'snippet': 'Her doctors thought the young woman had a virus commonly seen in children. But when she only got worse, one doctor looked elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': '“We’re going to the hospital,” the mother said to her 24-year-old daughter. The young woman had been crying in pain all night — and for the past three weeks. Her symptoms started with a couple of days of nonstop vomiting and a fever of 103. The vomiting stopped, but the fever continued. Then she broke out in a rash on her hands and feet. That’s when the pain started. First her right knee became stiff and swollen. Then her wrists and ankles. And soon after that, everything hurt.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 551, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 551}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-jumbo.png', 'height': 940, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 1881, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-thumbStandard.png', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-thumbStandard.png', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/magazine/02mag-Diagnosis-1/02mag-Diagnosis-1-thumbLarge.png', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Rash on Her Palms and the Bottoms of Her Feet Was the Clue That Turned the Case', 'kicker': 'Diagnosis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Rash on Her Palms and the Bottoms of Her Feet Was the Clue That Turned the Case', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hand, Foot and Mouth Disease', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-29T10:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lisa Sanders, M.D', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lisa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sanders', 'qualifier': 'M.D', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/456fbf25-873b-5fb8-9700-bca4ff9f1553', 'word_count': 1378, 'uri': 'nyt://article/456fbf25-873b-5fb8-9700-bca4ff9f1553'}, {'abstract': 'In India’s Pink City, the streets are filled with palaces, temples and, sometimes, cows. Eat like royalty, shop for jewelry and find a weekend’s worth of bliss amid the commotion.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/29/travel/what-to-do-in-jaipur.html', 'snippet': 'In India’s Pink City, the streets are filled with palaces, temples and, sometimes, cows. Eat like royalty, shop for jewelry and find a weekend’s worth of bliss amid the commotion.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nearly 300 years ago, an enlightened maharajah with a penchant for jewels and an eye for architecture built a planned city amid the arid hills of northwest India. Called Jaipur after the city’s founder, Jai Singh II, it arose on a grid of urban sectors not just for royal palaces, but for the workshops of artisans recruited to establish a new commercial hub. These days, gem cutters, jewelry designers and garment-makers are still flourishing in one of India’s most popular tourist and shopping destinations, part of the Delhi-Agra-Jaipur Golden Triangle. This is a city where the royals, to this day, occupy a wing of the City Palace, and where mid-rise towers and a new subway system are muscling in on a proud past. Street markets are awash in color and handicrafts, and Hindu temples can be found nearly every 100 yards. Though the streets seethe with beeping and belching traffic, tourists and dung-dropping cows, you can find bliss amid the commotion.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/travel/09hours/09hours-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/09/travel/09hours/09hours-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/travel/09hours/09hours-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/travel/09hours/09hours-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/09/travel/09hours/09hours-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'c