ll of Tekashi 6ix9ine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Rapper’s Antics Fueled Dizzying Ascent, Then Landed Him in Jail', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': '6ix9ine (Rapper)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rap and Hip-Hop', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Violence (Media and Entertainment)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'XXXTentacion (Rapper)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Organized Crime', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Racketeering and Racketeers', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-onlyinnewyork', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-29T10:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ali Watkins and Joe Coscarelli', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ali', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Watkins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Joe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Coscarelli', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c9246d26-b0ae-5d1a-8085-3db163770971', 'word_count': 2454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c9246d26-b0ae-5d1a-8085-3db163770971'}, {'abstract': 'The Tony-winning actress and frequent traveler talks about her favorite vacation spots, where she still wants to go (Bhutan and Tibet are on that list) and why she expects her hotel room to be ready when she arrives at her destination.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/29/travel/patti-lupone-interview-travel.html', 'snippet': 'The Tony-winning actress and frequent traveler talks about her favorite vacation spots, where she still wants to go (Bhutan and Tibet are on that list) and why she expects her hotel room to be ready when she arrives at her destination.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Patti LuPone entered into the annals of Broadway history when she appeared in the 1979 production of the Andrew Lloyd Webber musical, “Evita,” playing Eva Perón and winning the Tony Award that season for best actress in a musical. (In 2018, she gave a mesmerizing performance of that show’s “Don’t Cry for Me Argentina,” at the Grammy Awards, in tribute to Mr. Lloyd Webber, temporarily patching up a two-decade feud that dated back to when she was replaced by Glenn Close in the composer’s Broadway-bound musical “Sunset Boulevard.”)', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02qna-Lupone1/merlin_147081864_e6bda106-fb1e-4446-9895-983864903f9a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02qna-Lupone1/merlin_147081864_e6bda106-fb1e-4446-9895-983864903f9a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02qna-Lupone1/merlin_147081864_e6bda106-fb1e-4446-9895-983864903f9a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/travel/02qna-Lupone1/merlin_147081864_e6bda106-fb1e-4446-9895-983864903f9a-superJ