om/2018/11/29/us/politics/china-trump-cyberespionage.html', 'snippet': 'China’s practice of breaking into American computers has become a core grievance of the Trump administration as leaders of the two nations prepare to meet.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Three years ago, President Barack Obama struck a deal with China that few thought was possible: President Xi Jinping agreed to end his nation’s yearslong practice of breaking into the computer systems of American companies, military contractors and government agencies to obtain designs, technology and corporate secrets, usually on behalf of China’s state-owned firms.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/us/politics/30dc-cyber-1-print/merlin_147443805_1a40ea59-ae5a-477e-9f01-8605eae3d322-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/30/us/politics/30dc-cyber-1-print/merlin_147443805_1a40ea59-ae5a-477e-9f01-8605eae3d322-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/us/politics/30dc-cyber-1-print/merlin_147443805_1a40ea59-ae5a-477e-9f01-8605eae3d322-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/us/politics/30dc-cyber-1-print/merlin_147443805_1a40ea59-ae5a-477e-9f01-8605eae3d322-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/us/politics/30dc-cyber-1-print/29dc-cyber-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width