ng: The Fed’s Chair Sent the Markets Soaring', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Interest Rates', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-29T11:47:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24100480-d1fd-5b3a-b51c-15bd7684120c', 'word_count': 1781, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24100480-d1fd-5b3a-b51c-15bd7684120c'}, {'abstract': 'In the film, Paul Lieberstein plays a man who just needs to learn to scream. Viewers will feel his pain.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/29/movies/song-of-back-and-neck-review.html', 'snippet': 'In the film, Paul Lieberstein plays a man who just needs to learn to scream. Viewers will feel his pain.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Song of Back and Neck” tells the story of a paralegal who has repressed so much frustration that his anger has manifested in the form of chronic back and neck pain. Only acupuncture helps. And the needles in his back don’t merely vibrate; they make music, a phenomenon that turns him into a celebrity in the Chinese-American community. Broad cultural stereotyping is just one example of this movie’s dreary sense of humor.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/arts/song1/song1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/28/arts/song1/song1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'ra