py as Lazzaro,” Alice Rohrwacher’s mesmerizing new film, takes place in a rugged valley somewhere in central Italy. The residents, an extended clan of sharecroppers, grow tobacco, lentils and chickpeas on land belonging to an aristocratic family. No matter how hard they work, they are always in debt. Though there are a few signs of modernity — electric lights, motorized vehicles, a cellphone or two (but no signal), a Walkman — the feudal structure and pastoral rhythms of existence in this place, called Inviolata, seem timeless.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/arts/30Lazzaro/merlin_147232065_eec5980e-f867-4421-a119-f8fa9fff6562-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/30/arts/30Lazzaro/merlin_147232065_eec5980e-f867-4421-a119-f8fa9fff6562-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/arts/30Lazzaro/merlin_147232065_eec5980e-f867-4421-a119-f8fa9fff6562-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/arts/30Lazzaro/merlin_147232065_eec5980e-f867-4421-a119-f8fa9fff6562-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/arts/30Lazzaro/30Lazzaro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/30/arts/30Lazzaro/30Lazzaro-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbna