 is making work that is born out of, and that must on some level contend with, a culture that has turned food into fetish.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2018/11/29/t-magazine/in-images-artists-who-play-with-their-food.html', 'snippet': 'An emerging cohort is making work that is born out of, and that must on some level contend with, a culture that has turned food into fetish.', 'lead_paragraph': 'An emerging cohort is making work that is born out of, and that must on some level contend with, a culture that has turned food into fetish.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 447, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 447}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 764, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1527, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84/28tmag-foodart-slide-TE84-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Images: Artists Who Play With Their Food', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-11-29T16:09:08+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/20ce8db8-eeef-5016-b5e1-900db329384b', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/20ce8db8-eeef-5016-b5e1-900db329384b'}, {'abstract': 'For centuries, it’s been both medium and topic; now, an emerging cohort is challenging what it means to play with the most essential material.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/29/t-magazine/food-as-art.html', 'snippet': 'For centuries, it’s been both medium and topic; now, an emerging cohort is challenging what it means to play with the most essential material.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN THE PHOTOGRAPH, 16 raw yolks sit in a plastic ice-cube tray, each compartment brimming with albumen. Around the tray lie broken eggshells, cast off on a dimensionless blue surface. As a composition, it’s simple and striking, with saturated Jolly Rancher colors, the kind of image that pops on Instagram. But it doesn’t tell the story we’ve come to expect from food photographs that dominate social media: There’s no teasing promise of deliciousness or even edibility. The yolks are sunshine-yellow yet eerily rectangular, filling their ice-cube cells, which reflect the dimensions of the photograph itself. Nature has given way to artifice; shell has been separated from yolk, form from content, food from function. There’s nothing to eat here.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1252, 'width': 1877, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/28/t-magazine/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M/28tmag-foodart-slide-OO3M-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'These Artists Are Creating Work That’s About, and Made From, Food', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name'