stive Tract', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celiac Disease', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Crohn's Disease", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-30T10:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Eat', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roni Caryn Rabin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roni', 'middlename': 'Caryn', 'lastname': 'Rabin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/364ff2e4-569f-550c-a742-5ec680ca91bd', 'word_count': 326, 'uri': 'nyt://article/364ff2e4-569f-550c-a742-5ec680ca91bd'}, {'abstract': 'Readers will delight in the unexpected characters in three new mysteries, from the female police cadet in Louise Penny’s new book to a crime-solving cub reporter down on his luck.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/30/books/review/louise-penny-kingdom-of-the-blind.html', 'snippet': 'Readers will delight in the unexpected characters in three new mysteries, from the female police cadet in Louise Penny’s new book to a crime-solving cub reporter down on his luck.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The pretty Canadian village of Three Pines is slumbering peacefully through the “long, long, dark, dark, Québec winter” in Louise Penny’s latest mystery, KINGDOM OF THE BLIND (Minotaur, $28.99), when it is suddenly hit by a blizzard. The temperature drops to a chilling minus 35 degrees, snow blankets the village green and neighbors trudge through the towering drifts to warm themselves by the fireside at the local inn. But while the setting is entrancing, everyone knows that, “in the countryside, winter was a gorgeous, glorious, luminous killer.” And to prove that point, an old farmhouse collapses under the snow, trapping someone inside.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '49', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 1133, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 1133}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 543, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1085, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Crime/02Crime-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Buried by Snow or Stuffed in a Suitcase: The Bodies Add Up in Marilyn Stasio’s Latest Crime Column', 'kicker': 'Crime', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dead of Winter', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Kingdom of the Blind: A Chief Inspector Gamache Mystery (Book)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Penny, Louise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Bryant and May: Hall of Mirrors (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fowler, Christopher (1953- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Shadows We Hide (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eskens, Allen (1963- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Suitcase Charlie (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Guzlowski, John', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2018-11-30T10:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Marilyn Stasio', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Marilyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stasio', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff22bbb2-8910-5ae2-b836-5933e851a5e1', 'word_count': 851, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff22bbb2-8910-5ae2-b836-5933e851a5e1'}, {'abstract': 'Making sense of the president’s emotional state is now a media obsession, but how much is there really to understand?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/30/magazine/on-the-trump-mood-beat-but-why.html', 'snippet': 'Making sense of the president’s emotional state is now a media obsession, but how much is there really to understand?', 'lead_paragraph': '“Let’s start with the state of Donald Trump,” Fox News’s Chris Wallace said at the outset of the president’s latest on-camera interview, on Nov. 17, in the manner of a support-group facilitator pausing for a little check-in before an unpacking of recent events. “How dark is your mood?”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xla