, 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mark', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Leibovich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/073f50df-e122-5c29-aa56-06c9c2bb1114', 'word_count': 1171, 'uri': 'nyt://article/073f50df-e122-5c29-aa56-06c9c2bb1114'}, {'abstract': 'At least 79 pro-government forces were killed during the past week, as fighting spiked again, with another 54 civilians killed, many of them in air strikes and night raids.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/30/magazine/afghan-war-casualty-report.html', 'snippet': 'At least 79 pro-government forces were killed during the past week, as fighting spiked again, with another 54 civilians killed, many of them in air strikes and night raids.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The following reports compile all significant security incidents confirmed by New York Times reporters throughout Afghanistan. It is necessarily incomplete as many local officials refuse to confirm casualty information. The toll here does not generally include claims of insurgents killed by the government, because of the difficulty of verifying such claims. Similarly, the reports do not include attacks on the government claimed by the Taliban. Both sides routinely inflate casualties of their opponents. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/magazine/30atwar-casualty-report/merlin_147469104_1a90ed64-edd0-4635-a2b7-7af6dfe630b7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/11/30/magazine/30atwar-casualty-report/merlin_147469104_1a90ed64-edd0-4635-a2b7-7af6dfe630b7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/11/30/magaz