giving and concluded that no gift is as perfect as a book.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Notes From the Book Review Archives', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'From Our Archives', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2018-11-30T15:14:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/34e2f17f-2843-5e93-9969-b49d8b3a6c4f', 'word_count': 366, 'uri': 'nyt://article/34e2f17f-2843-5e93-9969-b49d8b3a6c4f'}, {'abstract': 'As the weather grows wetter and colder, it’s an excellent time to hole up with fantastical new fiction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2018/11/30/books/review/martha-wells-exit-strategy.html', 'snippet': 'As the weather grows wetter and colder, it’s an excellent time to hole up with fantastical new fiction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s that deepening part of autumn where darkness spreads wetter and colder, paving a path for winter and illness, and eliciting a general reluctance to leave one’s home. In other words, it’s an especially excellent time to hole up with some fantastic books, so here’s a roundup of recent robots, ghosts and a variety of monsters to take with one’s tea.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Otherworldly/merlin_146945889_f1a65efa-7a60-4004-b970-8f648326f658-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 636, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2018/12/02/books/review/02Otherworldly/merlin_146945889_f1a65efa-7a60-4004-b970-8f648326f658-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 